1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:02,368
So refreshing.

2
00:00:02,369 --> 00:00:03,971
(Bukit Lawang, Indonesia)

3
00:00:04,838 --> 00:00:06,372
The grass is longer here.

4
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:10,542
We're getting deeper into the jungle.

5
00:00:10,543 --> 00:00:11,710
The grass is longer.

6
00:00:11,711 --> 00:00:13,145
I see something...

7
00:00:13,146 --> 00:00:15,414
that looks like a fern
from the Paleozoic era.

8
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:16,883
Like this.

9
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:18,483
You're right.

10
00:00:18,484 --> 00:00:19,418
(They see unfamiliar plants.)

11
00:00:19,419 --> 00:00:22,655
Ipu, I want to see that grass.

12
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,390
When we touch it...

13
00:00:25,468 --> 00:00:27,235
When we touch it, it curls up.

14
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,427
It's not here.

15
00:00:28,428 --> 00:00:29,394
Not here?

16
00:00:29,395 --> 00:00:31,264
- Maybe we can look over there.
- Is that so?

17
00:00:31,265 --> 00:00:32,698
We have it in Korea.

18
00:00:34,101 --> 00:00:35,201
They don't have it here.

19
00:00:35,936 --> 00:00:37,437
Maybe they haven't found it.

20
00:00:37,438 --> 00:00:38,538
There's no way it doesn't grow here.

21
00:00:39,339 --> 00:00:41,374
- One minute, please.
- Okay.

22
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:42,275
One minute?

23
00:00:42,409 --> 00:00:43,176
- Are we done?
- Why?

24
00:00:43,177 --> 00:00:45,278
- Is he going home?
- Let me pick some of those leaves.

25
00:00:45,279 --> 00:00:46,913
He's going to pick that.

26
00:00:47,147 --> 00:00:48,214
- What's that?
- Amazing.

27
00:00:48,348 --> 00:00:49,915
Is he going to climb that tree?

28
00:00:50,093 --> 00:00:51,894
Is he going to shake that tree
and knock something down?

29
00:00:51,932 --> 00:00:52,719
(Jumping)

30
00:00:53,287 --> 00:00:54,588
(Ipu climbs the tree.)

31
00:00:54,589 --> 00:00:55,989
He's like Tarzan.

32
00:00:55,990 --> 00:00:57,223
That's really cool.

33
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:58,725
- Seriously.
- That's awesome.

34
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,026
That's the way to live.

35
00:01:01,929 --> 00:01:04,130
(Watching in awe)

36
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:10,036
(Skillfully picking a leaf)

37
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:13,439
You can tell that he loves this job.

38
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:14,373
That's really cool.

39
00:01:14,374 --> 00:01:15,841
He probably doesn't see it as work.

40
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:17,943
It's like introducing your home.

41
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,144
A room tour.

42
00:01:19,145 --> 00:01:20,312
He's giving us a room tour.

43
00:01:20,714 --> 00:01:22,715
He took us on a room tour.

44
00:01:22,716 --> 00:01:23,916
Ipu's room tour.

45
00:01:24,685 --> 00:01:25,885
Do you know what this is for?

46
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,687
- Do you know?
- Is that sugarcane?

47
00:01:28,857 --> 00:01:29,721
No.

48
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:31,390
- What is that?
- This can be used as a dye.

49
00:01:31,391 --> 00:01:32,424
Smooth?

50
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:34,393
- Smooth?
- For painting?

51
00:01:35,195 --> 00:01:36,428
You can dye things with this.

52
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:38,932
(They finally understand.)

53
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:40,333
Can I touch it?

54
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:42,034
- Maybe put it here.
- Okay.

55
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:43,336
Maybe here.

56
00:01:43,537 --> 00:01:46,239
(Rubbing it on a white cloth)

57
00:01:47,641 --> 00:01:50,443
(It dyes the cloth red!)

58
00:01:50,844 --> 00:01:52,478
Is it some kind of pigment?

59
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:54,213
A natural dye!

60
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:58,083
(The more he rubs it,
the darker the color gets.)

61
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,819
It will stay until you get back to Korea.

62
00:02:01,255 --> 00:02:02,655
Yes, I'm serious.

63
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,056
(The color holds up well!)

64
00:02:04,057 --> 00:02:05,057
That's okay.

65
00:02:05,158 --> 00:02:07,126
- Do you have another?
- Just one color?

66
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:08,026
One color.

67
00:02:08,562 --> 00:02:09,829
That's so interesting.

68
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,098
It's like a colored pencil.

69
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:14,033
That's fascinating.

70
00:02:14,034 --> 00:02:15,334
It's so much fun.

71
00:02:15,335 --> 00:02:16,902
This room tour is fun.

72
00:02:16,903 --> 00:02:18,637
- It's like a jungle adventure.
- I know.

73
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,206
This is not bad.

74
00:02:20,207 --> 00:02:21,373
It's pretty good so far.

75
00:02:21,374 --> 00:02:23,375
It's like a trekking route.

76
00:02:23,677 --> 00:02:24,944
If we keep going,

77
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:26,812
- we'll see monkeys...
- Yes.

78
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:29,215
- and orangutans too, right?
- I think so.

79
00:02:29,216 --> 00:02:31,817
The way to our lodging goes
through where orangutans live.

80
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:34,554
Here?

81
00:02:34,555 --> 00:02:37,256
We're visiting the orangutans' home, then.

82
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:40,158
There isn't a designated area
where they live.

83
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:42,528
No. They just roam freely in the wild.

84
00:02:42,529 --> 00:02:44,457
We can see them on our way to our place.

85
00:02:44,458 --> 00:02:45,711
(The whole jungle is their home.)

86
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,700
It feels like this is
where the jungle starts.

87
00:02:47,701 --> 00:02:49,935
I think we're entering the national park.

88
00:02:49,936 --> 00:02:51,870
(Arriving at the entrance
of the national park)

89
00:02:52,072 --> 00:02:53,839
Let's start trekking now.

90
00:02:54,275 --> 00:02:55,641
Okay, trekking!

91
00:02:55,642 --> 00:02:56,542
Let's go inside.

92
00:02:58,779 --> 00:03:00,813
It's getting started.

93
00:03:00,814 --> 00:03:02,615
That was just the intro so far.

94
00:03:02,616 --> 00:03:05,051
Let's look for orangutans and monkeys.

95
00:03:05,052 --> 00:03:07,186
- Okay!
- Okay!

96
00:03:07,454 --> 00:03:09,088
Let's just do it!

97
00:03:09,489 --> 00:03:10,889
Let's go.

98
00:03:11,959 --> 00:03:14,027
I'm walking in lunges,
squeezing my glutes.

99
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:15,994
It's a little muddy here.

100
00:03:16,396 --> 00:03:19,365
We're pretty used to mud now.

101
00:03:19,366 --> 00:03:20,232
Right.

102
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:22,568
The elephant hotel was muddy too.

103
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:25,004
We're very familiar with Mr. Mud now.

104
00:03:27,074 --> 00:03:28,541
- Mr. Mud?
- Yes.

105
00:03:28,809 --> 00:03:30,042
Mr. Mud,

106
00:03:30,944 --> 00:03:32,077
let's break up.

107
00:03:34,481 --> 00:03:36,481
(A random skit)

108
00:03:36,482 --> 00:03:37,550
I'm speechless.

109
00:03:39,353 --> 00:03:40,486
Mr. Mud.

110
00:03:41,121 --> 00:03:43,155
Mr. Mud, let's break up.

111
00:03:44,024 --> 00:03:45,324
Mr. Mud, I'm going to study abroad.

112
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:47,160
Stop following me.

113
00:03:47,161 --> 00:03:48,294
(Don't look for me.)

114
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,697
(Who are you?)

115
00:03:50,698 --> 00:03:51,531
That's so funny.

116
00:03:52,366 --> 00:03:53,533
Number Three seems to be struggling.

117
00:03:53,534 --> 00:03:55,168
No, I'm good.

118
00:03:55,169 --> 00:03:57,704
You look so tired from behind.

119
00:03:57,705 --> 00:03:59,439
(She looks exhausted from behind.)

120
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:01,250
Number Three, are you okay?

121
00:04:02,142 --> 00:04:03,409
Number Three isn't tired.

122
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:04,944
(The company commander is
disappointed in Number Three.)

123
00:04:05,113 --> 00:04:06,712
I'm so glad...

124
00:04:07,014 --> 00:04:08,247
that it's not blazing hot.

125
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,115
I agree.

126
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:12,318
If it was scorching hot,

127
00:04:12,319 --> 00:04:13,720
- I would've run away.
- I know.

128
00:04:14,121 --> 00:04:15,221
It's a real jungle.

129
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:17,690
(The slope gets steeper.)

130
00:04:17,691 --> 00:04:19,659
Now it's uphill.

131
00:04:20,387 --> 00:04:22,388
(Calling Ipu)

132
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:25,898
When did you start climbing trees?

133
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:29,168
Do you want to try?

134
00:04:29,670 --> 00:04:30,770
No.

135
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:31,738
That's not what she meant.

136
00:04:32,739 --> 00:04:33,739
Goodness.

137
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,641
Is he going to show us?

138
00:04:35,642 --> 00:04:36,508
Here.

139
00:04:36,509 --> 00:04:37,576
He's telling me to try.

140
00:04:37,577 --> 00:04:39,410
(Pushing through the grass,
straight to a tree)

141
00:04:41,348 --> 00:04:43,816
- Let's try it.
- I want to try climbing it.

142
00:04:43,817 --> 00:04:45,151
- You might be good at it.
- I think so too.

143
00:04:45,152 --> 00:04:46,152
You might be good.

144
00:04:47,187 --> 00:04:48,220
(The expert shows an example.)

145
00:04:48,221 --> 00:04:49,155
That looks like fun.

146
00:04:50,524 --> 00:04:51,924
I've always wanted to climb a tree.

147
00:04:51,925 --> 00:04:53,159
- Let's try it.
- Okay.

148
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,094
(Climbing the tree with bare hands)

149
00:04:55,929 --> 00:04:57,964
Let's go!

150
00:04:57,965 --> 00:04:59,031
Come up.

151
00:04:59,032 --> 00:05:00,099
(He reached the top quickly.)

152
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:01,733
Me too.

153
00:05:01,734 --> 00:05:04,470
Isn't there a limit
to how many people can climb the tree?

154
00:05:06,406 --> 00:05:07,339
- Amazing!
- How is it?

155
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:09,308
You're climbing well.

156
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,242
It's fun.

157
00:05:10,243 --> 00:05:11,844
How far up did he climb?

158
00:05:12,112 --> 00:05:13,646
(Relaxed)

159
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:16,882
She's so good at climbing.

160
00:05:18,285 --> 00:05:20,553
(She's already halfway up.)

161
00:05:20,554 --> 00:05:21,888
- This is crazy.
- She's a monkey.

162
00:05:22,355 --> 00:05:24,823
I'm so talented, right?

163
00:05:25,259 --> 00:05:26,395
Be careful.

164
00:05:26,396 --> 00:05:28,827
(She's talented in many ways.)

165
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:29,962
Let's go!

166
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:31,330
She's good at it.

167
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:35,067
(Singing)

168
00:05:35,788 --> 00:05:40,773
(She's talented like a monkey.)

169
00:05:41,241 --> 00:05:43,109
(She can dance while climbing a tree.)

170
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:44,376
Am I impressive?

171
00:05:45,545 --> 00:05:46,812
I'll go down.

172
00:05:48,682 --> 00:05:49,982
My lower body is so weak.

173
00:05:51,117 --> 00:05:53,819
(Sian gave up while flailing around.)

174
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:55,855
Are you going to go down that way?

175
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:57,423
(Pulling)

176
00:05:57,824 --> 00:05:58,690
Really?

177
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:04,062
(Tarzan)

178
00:06:04,464 --> 00:06:05,597
That's cool.

179
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,667
This is his playground.

180
00:06:09,236 --> 00:06:10,636
That's impressive.

181
00:06:10,637 --> 00:06:12,938
(He's basically one with the tree.)

182
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:14,373
Will Harimu do that too?

183
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:16,542
She should just come down, just in case.

184
00:06:16,543 --> 00:06:17,409
- Right.
- I'm scared for her.

185
00:06:17,778 --> 00:06:18,544
Okay.

186
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:19,545
(One step down)

187
00:06:19,570 --> 00:06:21,171
She's using her arms to climb down.

188
00:06:22,749 --> 00:06:24,616
(Turning)

189
00:06:24,617 --> 00:06:25,551
Watch out.

190
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:28,187
- Did you get any splinters?
- I'm good.

191
00:06:28,188 --> 00:06:30,088
That was fun, like pole dancing.

192
00:06:30,113 --> 00:06:31,214
Okay!

193
00:06:31,625 --> 00:06:32,959
- Okay!
- Okay!

194
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,460
I shouldn't have done that.

195
00:06:34,461 --> 00:06:35,462
My shoulder hurts.

196
00:06:35,463 --> 00:06:36,262
It hurts?

197
00:06:36,263 --> 00:06:37,230
I feel like it got a little twisted.

198
00:06:37,231 --> 00:06:39,198
- She did her best,
- I couldn't do it.

199
00:06:39,199 --> 00:06:41,367
but the talented one got
all our attention.

200
00:06:41,968 --> 00:06:43,101
She didn't get enough attention.

201
00:06:43,102 --> 00:06:44,236
I'm so talented, right?

202
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:45,804
She got the spotlight,

203
00:06:45,805 --> 00:06:47,973
- Right.
- so I gave up and came down.

204
00:06:47,974 --> 00:06:49,007
She did too well.

205
00:06:49,008 --> 00:06:51,243
She totally stole the spotlight.

206
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:52,544
Jane!

207
00:06:53,013 --> 00:06:54,313
Jane from "Tarzan."

208
00:06:55,982 --> 00:06:58,350
Is he talking about Jane from "Tarzan?"

209
00:06:58,351 --> 00:07:00,018
"Tarzan."

210
00:07:00,019 --> 00:07:02,454
I think he liked it.

211
00:07:03,924 --> 00:07:05,959
No, I'm a city girl.

212
00:07:08,328 --> 00:07:10,462
(Getting ahead of herself)

213
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:11,597
City girls!

214
00:07:11,598 --> 00:07:16,135
(The city girls' jungle trip continues.)

215
00:07:16,136 --> 00:07:17,136
By the way,

216
00:07:17,637 --> 00:07:19,207
I bet it feels so cool in the valley.

217
00:07:19,208 --> 00:07:20,673
- Seriously.
- Right?

218
00:07:20,674 --> 00:07:22,240
- I'd jump in.
- We don't even need bathing suits.

219
00:07:22,241 --> 00:07:23,342
We should jump right in.

220
00:07:23,343 --> 00:07:24,244
Right in the water.

221
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:27,179
I'm so happy
I haven't gotten any mosquito bites.

222
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:28,513
There's no sun either.

223
00:07:28,514 --> 00:07:29,648
(Jungle life is going pretty well.)

224
00:07:29,709 --> 00:07:31,043
Do you want to try sitting here?

225
00:07:31,265 --> 00:07:32,751
Climbing this tree?

226
00:07:32,752 --> 00:07:34,319
- A swing?
- That looks like a swing.

227
00:07:34,588 --> 00:07:35,855
A swing?

228
00:07:35,856 --> 00:07:38,157
(The tree branch is hanging down
like a swing.)

229
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:39,091
It's like a swing.

230
00:07:39,092 --> 00:07:40,459
How did the tree grow like this?

231
00:07:41,228 --> 00:07:42,528
A natural swing.

232
00:07:43,029 --> 00:07:43,795
Won Ji.

233
00:07:43,897 --> 00:07:44,864
Won Ji.

234
00:07:44,865 --> 00:07:46,565
- Won Ji.
- Grab that.

235
00:07:47,367 --> 00:07:48,267
Wait.

236
00:07:48,268 --> 00:07:50,169
It's getting interesting again.

237
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:51,737
No, I'll sit like a deity.

238
00:07:52,425 --> 00:07:54,092
Like the queen of this jungle.

239
00:07:54,708 --> 00:07:55,908
Okay!

240
00:07:55,909 --> 00:07:57,610
(Shutting her eyes tightly)

241
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:58,577
Wait.

242
00:07:58,745 --> 00:08:00,779
- Wait.
- Wait.

243
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:02,614
(Even Ipu realizes she's a scaredy-cat.)

244
00:08:02,615 --> 00:08:03,482
Harimu, try it.

245
00:08:05,185 --> 00:08:06,185
(Gasping)

246
00:08:06,186 --> 00:08:07,386
What did you just do?

247
00:08:08,222 --> 00:08:09,088
What's with me?

248
00:08:09,089 --> 00:08:10,356
(Curled up)

249
00:08:10,357 --> 00:08:11,757
Have fun, girl!

250
00:08:12,826 --> 00:08:13,692
I look like...

251
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,427
I'm pooping.

252
00:08:17,764 --> 00:08:19,498
- Okay!
- Okay!

253
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:20,599
(Won Ji's turn)

254
00:08:21,034 --> 00:08:23,469
Lift your feet. There you go!

255
00:08:23,470 --> 00:08:25,337
Her belly is shaking.

256
00:08:25,605 --> 00:08:27,639
Won Ji, engage your core.

257
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,576
(Who made her shake?)

258
00:08:30,577 --> 00:08:31,543
That's good.

259
00:08:31,544 --> 00:08:34,346
(Ipu shows off an advanced skill.)

260
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:37,015
- I want to try that too.
- Try it!

261
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:39,017
- I want to try that.
- Show me what you've got!

262
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:41,486
Make it, make it hot!
Show me what you've got!

263
00:08:41,487 --> 00:08:42,387
(It's Gabee's turn.)

264
00:08:42,388 --> 00:08:43,522
This might be really hard.

265
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,657
- Put your leg up there.
- Here?

266
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:46,792
I'll push it.

267
00:08:46,793 --> 00:08:48,660
(Hanging)

268
00:08:55,621 --> 00:08:57,536
You're doing well! There you go!

269
00:08:57,804 --> 00:08:58,617
You're the best!

270
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:03,275
(Screaming)

271
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:05,544
We're in the jungle!

272
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:07,580
(Showing all her pearly whites)

273
00:09:08,748 --> 00:09:09,782
(Gabee, way to go!)

274
00:09:09,783 --> 00:09:10,750
This is fun.

275
00:09:10,751 --> 00:09:12,385
- It's fun.
- It's so much fun.

276
00:09:12,386 --> 00:09:13,753
- It's really fun.
- Thank you.

277
00:09:13,754 --> 00:09:16,322
There are some activities here and there.

278
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:18,657
Now let's find some orangutans.

279
00:09:18,658 --> 00:09:19,592
- Okay.
- Okay.

280
00:09:19,593 --> 00:09:21,194
Let's focus and find the orangutans now.

281
00:09:21,219 --> 00:09:23,453
- Orangutans.
- Let's find the orangutans.

282
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:26,699
There's plenty of fun stuff to do...

283
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,567
besides looking for orangutans.

284
00:09:27,568 --> 00:09:29,968
His "What's in My Room" is so much fun.

285
00:09:30,337 --> 00:09:31,904
- "What's in My Room."
- "What's in My Room."

286
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:34,406
- "What's in My Room."
- He has so much fun stuff in his room.

287
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:35,841
Ipu's house tour.

288
00:09:35,842 --> 00:09:37,375
His house tour is so much fun.

289
00:09:37,844 --> 00:09:39,711
(Deeper into the rainforest)

290
00:09:39,712 --> 00:09:40,846
It's refreshing.

291
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:42,181
The shade.

292
00:09:43,403 --> 00:09:46,338
(Stepping over a fallen tree)

293
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,454
(Dodging all the vines
as they go deeper into the jungle)

294
00:09:48,455 --> 00:09:50,423
It's getting rougher and rougher.

295
00:09:51,192 --> 00:09:53,058
This is nothing like a regular hike.

296
00:09:53,059 --> 00:09:54,093
We keep having...

297
00:09:54,461 --> 00:09:56,228
- to step over trees.
- Right.

298
00:09:56,563 --> 00:09:58,597
This feels like a real jungle.

299
00:10:01,001 --> 00:10:02,067
This is great.

300
00:10:02,068 --> 00:10:02,689
Look.

301
00:10:03,090 --> 00:10:04,291
He's showing us something new.

302
00:10:04,292 --> 00:10:06,593
- Ipu's not even out of breath.
- A room tour.

303
00:10:06,594 --> 00:10:08,128
Ipu is a walking encyclopedia.

304
00:10:10,297 --> 00:10:11,039
(Orangutan call)

305
00:10:11,732 --> 00:10:12,325
(Surprised)

306
00:10:12,732 --> 00:10:14,134
- What?
- He found something.

307
00:10:15,012 --> 00:10:16,170
He must've found a monkey.

308
00:10:16,499 --> 00:10:17,519
- What?
- What?

309
00:10:17,579 --> 00:10:18,553
Isn't he calling them?

310
00:10:18,718 --> 00:10:20,359
It's an orangutan nest.

311
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,222
Really?

312
00:10:21,265 --> 00:10:22,924
- Where?
- There.

313
00:10:23,324 --> 00:10:24,893
- There?
- There it is.

314
00:10:25,018 --> 00:10:26,294
- That dark thing.
- Where?

315
00:10:27,195 --> 00:10:28,151
It's pretty high up.

316
00:10:28,152 --> 00:10:30,304
I only see the nest, not the orangutan.

317
00:10:30,478 --> 00:10:31,232
(Orangutan call)

318
00:10:32,267 --> 00:10:33,034
(Mimics the call)

319
00:10:33,778 --> 00:10:34,602
(Mimics the call)

320
00:10:35,303 --> 00:10:36,037
(Mimics the call)

321
00:10:36,538 --> 00:10:39,340
Can you see it? You know which one, right?
It's that dark thing.

322
00:10:39,625 --> 00:10:40,742
We'll see one soon.

323
00:10:40,885 --> 00:10:43,011
The monkey builds a nest.

324
00:10:43,012 --> 00:10:43,845
So cute.

325
00:10:43,898 --> 00:10:45,246
I can't wait to see an orangutan.

326
00:10:46,205 --> 00:10:47,048
Cute little orangutan.

327
00:10:47,612 --> 00:10:51,920
Will Mr. Orangutan stay up in the trees?

328
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:55,290
They're mostly in the trees,
but they come down too.

329
00:10:56,811 --> 00:10:58,526
We should watch the trees closely.

330
00:10:58,893 --> 00:11:00,962
I'll look up as we walk now.

331
00:11:02,363 --> 00:11:03,731
So smart.

332
00:11:03,771 --> 00:11:05,767
Brainy, so brainy. Really brainy.

333
00:11:05,768 --> 00:11:07,702
A brainy orangutan.

334
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:13,929
(Deeper into the mountain forest)

335
00:11:15,475 --> 00:11:16,211
(Orangutan call)

336
00:11:16,249 --> 00:11:18,379
(Repeated orangutan calls)

337
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:21,280
(Sian slips in an impersonation.)

338
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,218
- Nice.
- That sounded like an orangutan.

339
00:11:23,333 --> 00:11:25,119
You're good at impressions.

340
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:28,489
(Confident, she makes more ape calls.)

341
00:11:30,024 --> 00:11:32,126
- It's not easy.
- What do you mean, maybe not?

342
00:11:32,127 --> 00:11:33,718
(Maybe not)

343
00:11:34,896 --> 00:11:36,931
- He must've found something else.
- Why are we stopping?

344
00:11:37,111 --> 00:11:39,764
(Ipu suddenly stops.)

345
00:11:40,244 --> 00:11:42,377
I saw a mother orangutan and her baby.

346
00:11:42,378 --> 00:11:45,844
(Are they finally meeting an orangutan?)

347
00:11:45,891 --> 00:11:47,008
(Really?)

348
00:11:47,976 --> 00:11:49,110
He is serious.

349
00:11:49,111 --> 00:11:50,458
(Determined)

350
00:11:50,485 --> 00:11:52,614
Let's follow Ipu.

351
00:11:56,184 --> 00:11:57,785
It's completely muddy.

352
00:11:58,186 --> 00:12:00,186
It's getting more like a jungle.

353
00:12:01,169 --> 00:12:02,263
(Looking around)

354
00:12:02,603 --> 00:12:04,483
(Looking around)

355
00:12:04,929 --> 00:12:08,823
(There's an orangutan somewhere nearby.)

356
00:12:11,394 --> 00:12:14,269
Our Tarzan has stopped.

357
00:12:14,307 --> 00:12:15,236
My gosh.

358
00:12:15,997 --> 00:12:17,771
(Shushing)

359
00:12:18,367 --> 00:12:20,794
(Startled)

360
00:12:20,941 --> 00:12:22,110
There's an orangutan nearby.

361
00:12:22,111 --> 00:12:24,067
(Is it nearby?)

362
00:12:24,621 --> 00:12:26,241
(Over there)

363
00:12:26,734 --> 00:12:30,693
(They quietly begin the pursuit.)

364
00:12:32,373 --> 00:12:34,389
I think I hear something.

365
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:36,991
Slowly.

366
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:44,171
(Carefully, one step at a time)

367
00:12:45,667 --> 00:12:47,335
That's the person we saw earlier.

368
00:12:47,931 --> 00:12:50,417
(Startled)

369
00:12:50,784 --> 00:12:52,106
I'm sorry.

370
00:12:52,917 --> 00:12:53,808
Hello.

371
00:12:54,177 --> 00:12:57,156
(So happy to see the safety officer
from the entrance)

372
00:12:57,157 --> 00:12:59,116
(I can't with you.)

373
00:12:59,169 --> 00:13:00,581
He told us to be quiet.

374
00:13:01,182 --> 00:13:03,351
We're being quiet now.

375
00:13:05,229 --> 00:13:06,154
Sorry.

376
00:13:06,729 --> 00:13:07,755
I'm bad at reading the room.

377
00:13:09,123 --> 00:13:13,161
I feel like they'll be with us
until tomorrow.

378
00:13:13,428 --> 00:13:17,432
I saw him behind us,
but he keeps appearing ahead.

379
00:13:18,514 --> 00:13:20,435
It's wild. We keep running into him.

380
00:13:20,436 --> 00:13:22,338
(They resume their trek.)

381
00:13:23,778 --> 00:13:26,138
(Ipu suddenly seems to be in a hurry.)

382
00:13:28,198 --> 00:13:29,344
There must be one.

383
00:13:30,745 --> 00:13:32,313
No way.

384
00:13:32,425 --> 00:13:33,715
It's there.

385
00:13:34,015 --> 00:13:35,550
No, it's there. Over there.

386
00:13:35,705 --> 00:13:37,198
It's right there.

387
00:13:38,458 --> 00:13:40,792
(A glimpse of brown)

388
00:13:40,998 --> 00:13:42,156
Where?

389
00:13:42,345 --> 00:13:43,725
- We can go.
- He says to go.

390
00:13:43,752 --> 00:13:44,826
(Beckoning them over)

391
00:13:45,093 --> 00:13:46,728
Let's go.

392
00:13:47,312 --> 00:13:48,162
Let's go.

393
00:13:49,063 --> 00:13:51,466
They're easier to see than I expected.

394
00:13:52,539 --> 00:13:54,873
(Slowly moving higher)

395
00:13:57,346 --> 00:13:59,440
We're really close now.

396
00:14:00,291 --> 00:14:01,376
Here.

397
00:14:01,917 --> 00:14:02,710
Where?

398
00:14:02,864 --> 00:14:04,864
- Here.
- Is it there?

399
00:14:04,865 --> 00:14:07,318
(Thick fur visible through the trees)

400
00:14:07,385 --> 00:14:08,316
There it is.

401
00:14:08,478 --> 00:14:09,317
Amazing!

402
00:14:09,917 --> 00:14:11,486
This is incredible.

403
00:14:11,872 --> 00:14:13,654
- This is amazing.
- Totally.

404
00:14:13,945 --> 00:14:14,822
Let's go.

405
00:14:14,823 --> 00:14:17,217
(They decide to move closer.)

406
00:14:20,728 --> 00:14:22,730
There are two of them.

407
00:14:24,832 --> 00:14:26,860
- Two?
- There are two.

408
00:14:27,286 --> 00:14:28,469
They're so cute.

409
00:14:28,470 --> 00:14:29,804
Are they mother and baby?

410
00:14:33,639 --> 00:14:40,508
(At last, their first orangutan encounter)

411
00:14:43,435 --> 00:14:45,242
- A baby.
- A baby.

412
00:14:45,542 --> 00:14:46,721
A baby and its mother.

413
00:14:46,808 --> 00:14:48,189
A mother and baby.

414
00:14:49,891 --> 00:14:50,858
So cute.

415
00:14:51,206 --> 00:14:52,059
So cute.

416
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:54,566
(A baby orangutan with its mother)

417
00:14:57,006 --> 00:14:58,466
- So cute.
- Hello.

418
00:14:58,467 --> 00:14:59,553
(Flailing)

419
00:15:00,446 --> 00:15:02,020
(Dangling)

420
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:03,304
- Hey there.
- Hi!

421
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,809
Its messy hair is just my style.

422
00:15:08,865 --> 00:15:09,710
So cute.

423
00:15:10,077 --> 00:15:12,847
This is incredible. I never thought
we'd see one this close.

424
00:15:12,848 --> 00:15:15,411
(Its charmingly messy hair)

425
00:15:15,465 --> 00:15:16,417
Hello.

426
00:15:16,531 --> 00:15:18,653
So cute.
It seems to be saying hello to me.

427
00:15:21,011 --> 00:15:21,989
It's peeing.

428
00:15:22,211 --> 00:15:23,191
(Trickling)

429
00:15:23,745 --> 00:15:25,092
It seems to be saying hello.

430
00:15:25,705 --> 00:15:26,561
Hello.

431
00:15:26,562 --> 00:15:28,965
(Peeing instead of saying hello)

432
00:15:29,297 --> 00:15:30,945
There's a baby too.

433
00:15:30,946 --> 00:15:33,505
(A fascinating sight)

434
00:15:33,566 --> 00:15:34,802
Where did the big one go?

435
00:15:35,519 --> 00:15:36,871
It climbed higher.

436
00:15:37,599 --> 00:15:38,706
It's avoiding us.

437
00:15:39,574 --> 00:15:41,574
I think it avoids us because we're human.

438
00:15:41,705 --> 00:15:42,944
This is fascinating.

439
00:15:46,545 --> 00:15:47,799
(Scratching)

440
00:15:47,825 --> 00:15:48,683
It's scratching.

441
00:15:49,639 --> 00:15:51,052
Scratch, scratch.

442
00:15:52,025 --> 00:15:53,621
Its hands are really big.

443
00:15:55,705 --> 00:15:57,325
Its hands are huge.

444
00:15:58,265 --> 00:15:59,861
I can't take my eyes off it.

445
00:15:59,979 --> 00:16:00,962
It pooped.

446
00:16:01,179 --> 00:16:01,996
Poop?

447
00:16:02,432 --> 00:16:03,397
It pooped.

448
00:16:03,724 --> 00:16:04,665
The baby pooped.

449
00:16:04,666 --> 00:16:05,900
Again. Look.

450
00:16:05,952 --> 00:16:07,401
(Plopping)

451
00:16:07,552 --> 00:16:09,370
- Its poop is green.
- You're right.

452
00:16:09,485 --> 00:16:10,371
Is that pee?

453
00:16:10,619 --> 00:16:12,473
Or maybe it's dropping fruit.

454
00:16:12,474 --> 00:16:13,441
Fruit.

455
00:16:13,725 --> 00:16:14,876
(Dropping food as it eats)

456
00:16:14,877 --> 00:16:15,877
Fascinating.

457
00:16:16,352 --> 00:16:17,445
Hello.

458
00:16:17,765 --> 00:16:19,981
Hello. Nice to meet you.

459
00:16:21,315 --> 00:16:23,315
I'm from Korea.

460
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:26,787
It's looking down.

461
00:16:30,246 --> 00:16:31,726
We're fascinated by each other.

462
00:16:31,946 --> 00:16:33,027
This is fascinating.

463
00:16:33,806 --> 00:16:35,029
Should we take a photo together?

464
00:16:36,633 --> 00:16:38,065
- It's close.
- Can you see it?

465
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,073
- It's here.
- Is it here?

466
00:16:40,086 --> 00:16:41,936
I think it's there. Or is that not it?

467
00:16:42,270 --> 00:16:43,204
I think that's it.

468
00:16:43,205 --> 00:16:47,178
(The orangutan in the middle)

469
00:16:48,898 --> 00:16:51,212
Hello.

470
00:16:53,314 --> 00:16:55,950
- This is amazing.
- We even watched them eat.

471
00:16:56,417 --> 00:16:59,153
The difference in size is enormous.

472
00:16:59,276 --> 00:17:02,329
- Exactly.
- The mom is huge, but the baby is tiny.

473
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:03,457
This is fascinating.

474
00:17:06,009 --> 00:17:08,663
It's amazing how he walks barefoot.

475
00:17:11,074 --> 00:17:14,940
(Carefully following Ipu)

476
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:17,672
There are monkeys.

477
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,053
- Monkeys?
- Yes.

478
00:17:19,354 --> 00:17:20,508
Another monkey?

479
00:17:20,898 --> 00:17:22,843
It's over there!

480
00:17:23,377 --> 00:17:24,378
That's a baby.

481
00:17:24,531 --> 00:17:25,646
A monkey is here?

482
00:17:25,647 --> 00:17:26,478
(Peeking out)

483
00:17:26,945 --> 00:17:28,215
There's a monkey?

484
00:17:28,616 --> 00:17:30,685
- So cute.
- It's close.

485
00:17:30,731 --> 00:17:32,119
It's passing in front of us.

486
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,378
(A pig-tailed macaque)

487
00:17:34,188 --> 00:17:36,591
It's not the same kind as earlier.

488
00:17:37,291 --> 00:17:38,492
It's just a baby.

489
00:17:38,965 --> 00:17:40,328
So freaking cute.

490
00:17:40,478 --> 00:17:42,263
We're seeing many moms and babies today.

491
00:17:42,472 --> 00:17:44,065
And what's so cute is...

492
00:17:44,152 --> 00:17:47,068
- it touches the tree before going.
- Before crossing?

493
00:17:47,192 --> 00:17:50,070
- Like testing a bridge?
- Look before you leap.

494
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:52,340
Shake a tree before climbing it.

495
00:17:53,163 --> 00:17:54,942
So cute.

496
00:17:54,943 --> 00:17:56,043
- My goodness.
- So cute.

497
00:17:56,044 --> 00:17:57,603
(An adorable baby monkey)

498
00:17:58,112 --> 00:17:59,847
It eats things off the tree.

499
00:18:00,183 --> 00:18:02,183
I can't handle how cute it is.

500
00:18:02,203 --> 00:18:03,351
I can't handle this.

501
00:18:03,397 --> 00:18:04,685
It's so cute.

502
00:18:05,342 --> 00:18:06,654
It looks just like a person.

503
00:18:06,702 --> 00:18:08,422
Its ears and ribs too.

504
00:18:09,657 --> 00:18:12,526
Our guide Ipu...

505
00:18:12,610 --> 00:18:13,309
(Monkey call)

506
00:18:13,310 --> 00:18:15,563
is great at spotting monkeys.

507
00:18:15,564 --> 00:18:16,397
(Monkey call)

508
00:18:17,977 --> 00:18:19,100
(Monkey call)

509
00:18:19,567 --> 00:18:20,534
(Imitating the call)

510
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:21,936
(Monkey call)

511
00:18:21,997 --> 00:18:22,950
(Imitating the call)

512
00:18:22,964 --> 00:18:23,871
(Monkey call)

513
00:18:24,017 --> 00:18:24,939
(Imitating the call)

514
00:18:25,884 --> 00:18:29,110
But Ipu is amazing.
How does he know this path?

515
00:18:29,184 --> 00:18:30,511
- Right.
- He knows it by heart?

516
00:18:31,245 --> 00:18:33,447
He memorized every path.
That's so impressive.

517
00:18:33,508 --> 00:18:35,182
He must come here all the time, right?

518
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:42,446
(Did Ipu find something else?)

519
00:18:43,282 --> 00:18:43,891
What is it?

520
00:18:43,993 --> 00:18:46,460
Why are you standing so solemnly, Ipu?

521
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:48,829
You startled me.

522
00:18:48,952 --> 00:18:49,797
What is it?

523
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:50,965
There must be something.

524
00:18:51,732 --> 00:18:52,833
What is it?

525
00:18:53,446 --> 00:18:54,635
What is it this time?

526
00:18:58,312 --> 00:18:59,440
That scared me.

527
00:18:59,441 --> 00:19:02,212
(Could something be wrong?)

528
00:19:02,792 --> 00:19:05,012
(Watching him carefully)

529
00:19:05,659 --> 00:19:06,814
You can eat fruit here.

530
00:19:08,779 --> 00:19:10,217
It must be time to eat fruit.

531
00:19:10,218 --> 00:19:11,499
(That's it?)

532
00:19:11,826 --> 00:19:15,159
But he sounded so serious saying it.

533
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:16,257
That was scary.

534
00:19:16,258 --> 00:19:17,625
I thought there was a tiger.

535
00:19:18,305 --> 00:19:21,859
(The impersonation begins.)

536
00:19:22,246 --> 00:19:24,331
Eat fruit.

537
00:19:25,573 --> 00:19:27,306
It's very hot.

538
00:19:27,359 --> 00:19:29,103
- "It's very hot, so come over here?"
- It's very hot?

539
00:19:29,157 --> 00:19:31,472
This is so funny.

540
00:19:31,872 --> 00:19:33,340
I'm losing it.

541
00:19:33,941 --> 00:19:34,842
"Very hot."

542
00:19:35,297 --> 00:19:36,844
Ipu is my type of guy.

543
00:19:37,611 --> 00:19:40,548
Which one of Ipu's rooms is this?

544
00:19:40,848 --> 00:19:43,017
- The 20th.
- The 20th?

545
00:19:43,136 --> 00:19:45,286
- He keeps searching for things.
- Exactly.

546
00:19:46,056 --> 00:19:47,488
How can he even see that?

547
00:19:48,363 --> 00:19:50,725
Just seeing this is incredible.

548
00:19:51,214 --> 00:19:52,359
And he keeps making this face.

549
00:19:53,728 --> 00:19:54,895
You're good at that.

550
00:19:54,896 --> 00:19:56,468
(Serious)

551
00:19:56,561 --> 00:19:57,665
That's good.

552
00:19:59,081 --> 00:20:00,914
Eat fruit.

553
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:04,836
(Ipu has a character.)

554
00:20:05,972 --> 00:20:09,507
- This is so funny.
- He's different when looking at us...

555
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:11,343
compared to when he's looking
for an orangutan.

556
00:20:11,344 --> 00:20:12,744
He goes like this.

557
00:20:12,745 --> 00:20:13,645
He's good at his job.

558
00:20:14,113 --> 00:20:15,713
I have some fruit for you.

559
00:20:16,082 --> 00:20:17,549
(Finally, it's break time!)

560
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:18,717
What kind of fruit?

561
00:20:18,718 --> 00:20:20,685
I have some bananas, oranges,

562
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,454
passion fruit,

563
00:20:22,455 --> 00:20:24,556
pineapple,

564
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:25,657
and dragon fruit.

565
00:20:25,658 --> 00:20:27,559
Dragon fruit!

566
00:20:27,793 --> 00:20:29,327
That's quite a variety.

567
00:20:29,595 --> 00:20:32,330
He's even setting up seats for us
with the banana leaf.

568
00:20:32,331 --> 00:20:33,164
The banana leaf...

569
00:20:35,601 --> 00:20:38,403
(Eco-friendly sitting mat)

570
00:20:38,638 --> 00:20:40,539
I don't think that's our seat.

571
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,740
It's probably going to be our dish.

572
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:42,941
Oh, a dish.

573
00:20:42,942 --> 00:20:44,343
A fruit dish.

574
00:20:44,577 --> 00:20:46,077
That's how it was when I looked it up.

575
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:48,046
- See? Research is important.
- I've seen it.

576
00:20:48,047 --> 00:20:49,514
- It's usually for the plate.
- I see.

577
00:20:49,515 --> 00:20:51,283
We almost sat on it.

578
00:20:51,284 --> 00:20:52,484
(Fruit dish almost became butt dish.)

579
00:20:54,286 --> 00:20:56,220
(Rustle)

580
00:20:56,322 --> 00:20:57,255
I see a monkey!

581
00:20:57,457 --> 00:20:59,757
Maybe he smelled the fruit.

582
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:00,858
There he is.

583
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:02,760
- Where do you see them?
- Over there.

584
00:21:02,761 --> 00:21:03,795
I see him.

585
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:05,830
He has gray fur.

586
00:21:05,831 --> 00:21:08,934
I see another species.

587
00:21:09,535 --> 00:21:10,802
He looks like he's wearing a mask.

588
00:21:10,803 --> 00:21:12,871
He's leaning his head on the tree.

589
00:21:13,406 --> 00:21:15,073
He's so cute.
He looks like a penguin.

590
00:21:15,074 --> 00:21:16,108
(Spotted a surprisingly stylish monkey)

591
00:21:16,409 --> 00:21:19,210
He kind of looks like he's wearing
a Muay Thai mask.

592
00:21:19,412 --> 00:21:20,779
He reminds me of "King of Masked Singer."

593
00:21:20,913 --> 00:21:23,781
(Chuckle)

594
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:26,118
He kind of does.

595
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:28,486
He can definitely enter
"King of Masked Singer."

596
00:21:28,487 --> 00:21:29,858
(Thomas's langur: endemic
to northern Sumatra,)

597
00:21:29,859 --> 00:21:31,256
(known for mask-like facial markings.)

598
00:21:31,423 --> 00:21:32,790
His tail is super long.

599
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:34,993
Right.

600
00:21:34,994 --> 00:21:36,494
He has a long tail.

601
00:21:36,495 --> 00:21:38,830
His tail is longer than his body.

602
00:21:39,398 --> 00:21:40,632
He looks so mysterious.

603
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:42,200
He's beautiful.

604
00:21:42,201 --> 00:21:44,569
How do you say "long tail" in Korean?

605
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:46,838
"Gin kkori."

606
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:48,786
"Gin kkori wonsungi."

607
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:50,174
"Gin kkori wonsungi."

608
00:21:51,077 --> 00:21:53,378
Your pronunciation is very good.

609
00:21:54,547 --> 00:21:55,881
Ipu's pronunciation is so good.

610
00:21:56,315 --> 00:22:00,652
(He can traverse the jungle
with a tail longer than his body.)

611
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,653
Come this way.

612
00:22:02,055 --> 00:22:03,522
Ipu's telling us to come.

613
00:22:03,856 --> 00:22:07,125
- Let's go.
- He's so cute.

614
00:22:07,626 --> 00:22:08,693
Oh my god!

615
00:22:08,861 --> 00:22:10,528
He's right in front of us.
How cute.

616
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:14,333
- He seems shy.
- His tail is super long.

617
00:22:14,334 --> 00:22:16,000
The way he's perched is so cute.

618
00:22:16,001 --> 00:22:18,770
(Saying hello up close.)

619
00:22:19,105 --> 00:22:20,405
His head is so small.

620
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:22,607
Doesn't he remind you of Sun Wukong?

621
00:22:22,608 --> 00:22:23,909
He looks like a character
from "Romance of the Three Kingdoms."

622
00:22:23,910 --> 00:22:25,376
I think it's his hair.

623
00:22:25,377 --> 00:22:27,479
He has an edgy hairstyle.

624
00:22:27,780 --> 00:22:28,913
He kind of does.

625
00:22:28,914 --> 00:22:29,781
I like it.

626
00:22:29,782 --> 00:22:32,083
His hairstyle is cool.

627
00:22:32,084 --> 00:22:34,352
- He must groom himself well.
- He has a mohawk hairstyle.

628
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:36,087
He's very cool. So funky.

629
00:22:36,622 --> 00:22:37,488
Let's go back.

630
00:22:37,723 --> 00:22:41,025
I think our fruit is almost ready.

631
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:42,326
Let's go.

632
00:22:42,895 --> 00:22:44,162
That was so cute.

633
00:22:44,163 --> 00:22:45,096
Right, he was so cute.

634
00:22:45,498 --> 00:22:47,065
Oh, we meet again.

635
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:48,900
Won Ji, he's here again.

636
00:22:49,335 --> 00:22:50,669
- He's Won Ji's favorite.
- Just a second.

637
00:22:51,104 --> 00:22:52,703
I'm going to interview him.

638
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:53,904
How are you?

639
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:55,340
What's your name?

640
00:22:55,341 --> 00:22:56,841
(Puzzled)

641
00:22:56,842 --> 00:22:57,809
John.

642
00:22:57,810 --> 00:22:59,644
- Are you from Indonesia?
- Yes.

643
00:23:00,279 --> 00:23:01,713
Are you part of our team?

644
00:23:02,014 --> 00:23:06,851
Yeah, I'm the park security here.

645
00:23:07,119 --> 00:23:09,754
We met three times, remember?

646
00:23:09,755 --> 00:23:10,755
Yeah.

647
00:23:11,624 --> 00:23:14,226
- So that's why he was everywhere.
- He was the security.

648
00:23:14,760 --> 00:23:16,527
- You're the security.
- The security.

649
00:23:17,329 --> 00:23:19,297
Thank you so much.

650
00:23:19,298 --> 00:23:20,431
Thank you.

651
00:23:20,633 --> 00:23:22,500
Finally, the mystery solves itself.

652
00:23:22,501 --> 00:23:24,369
I thought he was part of our team.

653
00:23:25,604 --> 00:23:28,573
(The fruits are still being prepared.)

654
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:31,210
(Rustle)

655
00:23:31,211 --> 00:23:32,710
Look, look!

656
00:23:32,711 --> 00:23:34,712
- The monkey came.
- They must be here for the fruit.

657
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:37,048
- Do you think it's the same one?
- Let's invite them over.

658
00:23:37,049 --> 00:23:38,049
Oh, it's peeing.

659
00:23:39,118 --> 00:23:40,919
It would be so funny if it peed here.

660
00:23:41,387 --> 00:23:42,587
Is it the same monkey from before?

661
00:23:43,222 --> 00:23:45,390
It must have smelled the fruit.

662
00:23:45,391 --> 00:23:47,325
It's practically drooling already.

663
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,693
Hey, don't poop here, okay?

664
00:23:49,862 --> 00:23:51,229
There are some monkeys above us too.

665
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:52,697
There are so many.

666
00:23:52,965 --> 00:23:54,999
They must have smelled our fruit.

667
00:23:55,401 --> 00:23:56,634
It's super crowded up there.

668
00:23:56,769 --> 00:23:58,436
They must be waiting until we leave.

669
00:23:58,571 --> 00:24:01,039
They're waiting for our leftovers.

670
00:24:01,407 --> 00:24:02,540
"Slurp."

671
00:24:04,977 --> 00:24:06,110
Look over there!

672
00:24:06,412 --> 00:24:07,278
Where?

673
00:24:08,514 --> 00:24:09,681
We're surrounded.

674
00:24:10,316 --> 00:24:11,783
There's one there...

675
00:24:11,784 --> 00:24:12,717
and another over there.

676
00:24:13,152 --> 00:24:15,920
- Look over there.
- We're surrounded.

677
00:24:16,087 --> 00:24:17,588
I think I see a baby monkey.

678
00:24:19,325 --> 00:24:20,692
There's a baby over there.

679
00:24:21,193 --> 00:24:23,294
How young do you think it is?
Looks very young.

680
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:25,897
It's right next to her.

681
00:24:26,799 --> 00:24:27,799
Look at the baby.

682
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:28,900
(Fluffy baby monkey)

683
00:24:28,901 --> 00:24:31,302
- So small.
- They're so cute.

684
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:32,236
Super cute.

685
00:24:33,272 --> 00:24:34,872
How adorable.

686
00:24:35,507 --> 00:24:36,507
Such a baby, right?

687
00:24:37,409 --> 00:24:39,210
Could it be a newborn?

688
00:24:40,179 --> 00:24:41,246
I see one over there, too.

689
00:24:41,247 --> 00:24:42,114
(Amazed)

690
00:24:42,115 --> 00:24:43,081
So cute.

691
00:24:43,249 --> 00:24:44,549
The baby monkey...

692
00:24:44,550 --> 00:24:46,251
is so cute.

693
00:24:46,252 --> 00:24:47,084
(Amazed and excited)

694
00:24:47,085 --> 00:24:47,986
There's one over there, too.

695
00:24:49,054 --> 00:24:50,788
This is so amazing.

696
00:24:50,789 --> 00:24:54,025
(Slipping back to mom's arms)

697
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:55,593
Now, let's eat the fruit.

698
00:24:55,895 --> 00:24:56,794
Wow.

699
00:24:57,763 --> 00:24:58,863
This is so pretty.

700
00:24:59,798 --> 00:25:01,932
The watermelon's so red.

701
00:25:02,301 --> 00:25:03,935
The colors are beautiful.

702
00:25:03,936 --> 00:25:04,902
Look at the watermelon.

703
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:06,070
I see mandarin oranges, too.

704
00:25:06,071 --> 00:25:07,272
(Colors blended by nature)

705
00:25:07,273 --> 00:25:09,007
It's so pretty.

706
00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:11,976
Look, he sandwiched passionfruit
between pineapple slices.

707
00:25:12,445 --> 00:25:13,511
True foodie.

708
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:15,259
(He knows what he's doing
as a legendary foodie.)

709
00:25:15,259 --> 00:25:17,052
"True foodie."

710
00:25:17,249 --> 00:25:18,783
A culinary genius.

711
00:25:18,784 --> 00:25:20,985
This is so refreshing.

712
00:25:21,453 --> 00:25:23,020
We have oranges and bananas.

713
00:25:23,021 --> 00:25:25,189
How pretty.

714
00:25:25,325 --> 00:25:26,825
They took such care.

715
00:25:26,826 --> 00:25:27,859
(Decorated with flowers.)

716
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:29,361
The colors are arranged so beautifully.

717
00:25:29,962 --> 00:25:31,362
So pretty.

718
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:33,064
(Almost too pretty to eat)

719
00:25:33,065 --> 00:25:34,899
You can eat now.

720
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:37,335
- Thank you!
- Thank you for the fruit.

721
00:25:37,603 --> 00:25:40,438
Watermelons are my favorite.

722
00:25:40,973 --> 00:25:43,007
(Chomp)

723
00:25:43,842 --> 00:25:44,842
This is so sweet.

724
00:25:45,544 --> 00:25:46,677
Getting my daily dose of vitamins!

725
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:48,780
It's incredibly sweet.

726
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:51,482
The pineapple-passionfruit sandwich
is so good.

727
00:25:51,817 --> 00:25:53,417
Pineapples are so tangy.

728
00:25:53,418 --> 00:25:54,285
It's good, right?

729
00:25:54,286 --> 00:25:56,487
- It's very refreshing.
- He's indeed a foodie expert.

730
00:25:57,589 --> 00:26:00,624
(Getting proper vitamins)

731
00:26:01,093 --> 00:26:04,662
(Some fruit for Ipu
after all his hard work.)

732
00:26:04,663 --> 00:26:05,396
Ipu,

733
00:26:05,698 --> 00:26:07,332
can I have one mandarin orange?

734
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:09,867
Just one.

735
00:26:11,437 --> 00:26:12,937
He gave me two.

736
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,138
Do you want some?

737
00:26:14,139 --> 00:26:17,007
(Resorts to stealing fruit
because it's so good.)

738
00:26:18,477 --> 00:26:19,610
The mandarin orange is so delicious.

739
00:26:20,946 --> 00:26:22,546
I feel recharged.

740
00:26:24,316 --> 00:26:25,716
Do you want to try this one, too?

741
00:26:25,717 --> 00:26:27,418
I want to try.

742
00:26:27,853 --> 00:26:28,853
Thank you.

743
00:26:28,854 --> 00:26:29,720
What is it?

744
00:26:30,055 --> 00:26:31,689
That's snake fruit.

745
00:26:31,957 --> 00:26:34,162
(Salak: a tropical fruit
often called snakefruit...)

746
00:26:34,163 --> 00:26:35,693
(due to its scaly skin.)

747
00:26:35,861 --> 00:26:37,929
How do we eat this? Do we just peel it?

748
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:39,597
Oh, you just peel it.

749
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:41,299
(White flesh exposed when peeled off)

750
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:43,034
Like garlic?

751
00:26:43,202 --> 00:26:44,936
(Chomp after making it bite-sized)

752
00:26:44,937 --> 00:26:45,770
Okay.

753
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:48,606
- Do we put the peels here?
- Yeah.

754
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:49,407
Okay.

755
00:26:49,942 --> 00:26:50,875
It's delicious.

756
00:26:51,577 --> 00:26:52,443
Do you want to try?

757
00:26:52,578 --> 00:26:53,478
It smells nice.

758
00:26:53,979 --> 00:26:54,912
It's tangy.

759
00:26:54,913 --> 00:26:56,347
(Nom)

760
00:26:59,585 --> 00:27:01,619
It tastes like chestnuts but sour.

761
00:27:02,154 --> 00:27:04,355
Do you not like it? I like its aroma.

762
00:27:05,191 --> 00:27:06,324
You have to take out the seed.

763
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:09,895
(Chomp)

764
00:27:09,896 --> 00:27:11,563
The fruit inside is delicious.

765
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,231
Can this cause diarrhea?

766
00:27:14,232 --> 00:27:15,299
No, no.

767
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:16,333
It prevents diarrhea.

768
00:27:16,334 --> 00:27:17,735
So it's the opposite.

769
00:27:18,403 --> 00:27:20,138
When you have a stomachache,

770
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:21,239
eating this would stop it?

771
00:27:21,240 --> 00:27:23,107
So it works like anti-diarrhea medicine.

772
00:27:23,108 --> 00:27:24,208
Right.

773
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:25,342
I think it's a good idea to eat this.

774
00:27:25,343 --> 00:27:27,578
We would be in trouble if we need
to go number 2 in the jungle.

775
00:27:31,583 --> 00:27:33,117
Do you want to see a magic trick?

776
00:27:33,685 --> 00:27:36,020
(Bring it already.)

777
00:27:36,021 --> 00:27:37,354
He's going to show us a magic trick.

778
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:46,431
Is there anything he can't do?

779
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:50,467
What if all the monkeys gather around?

780
00:27:51,303 --> 00:27:52,336
Wow.

781
00:27:53,639 --> 00:27:54,872
It's magic plastic.

782
00:27:54,873 --> 00:27:56,374
He's really good.

783
00:27:56,375 --> 00:27:57,909
Ipu the piper.

784
00:27:57,910 --> 00:27:58,743
Wow.

785
00:27:58,744 --> 00:27:59,844
(Ipu can do anything.)

786
00:28:00,279 --> 00:28:01,980
Do you want to see another trick?

787
00:28:01,981 --> 00:28:03,581
Second magic trick?

788
00:28:04,116 --> 00:28:06,284
(Open)

789
00:28:08,821 --> 00:28:09,687
Where did he come from?

790
00:28:09,721 --> 00:28:10,521
(It's a snake!)

791
00:28:10,856 --> 00:28:12,990
It's a real snake.

792
00:28:13,093 --> 00:28:15,460
(Shocked)

793
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:16,594
Wow.

794
00:28:16,595 --> 00:28:19,864
(Snake engaging with his core)

795
00:28:20,265 --> 00:28:21,799
(Flicking his tongue.)

796
00:28:22,167 --> 00:28:24,368
Is it okay to do that?

797
00:28:25,037 --> 00:28:26,070
(Folding him neatly)

798
00:28:28,073 --> 00:28:28,973
(Ah)

799
00:28:28,974 --> 00:28:30,942
No, don't do that.

800
00:28:31,276 --> 00:28:32,476
Is it even safe?

801
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:35,546
(He put the snake in his mouth.)

802
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:36,614
Is he really doing this?

803
00:28:36,615 --> 00:28:38,201
(Do not attempt.)

804
00:28:38,202 --> 00:28:40,718
(This was filmed safely
with a trained professional.)

805
00:28:40,786 --> 00:28:43,789
(Shocked)

806
00:28:43,790 --> 00:28:44,756
That's crazy.

807
00:28:44,757 --> 00:28:46,724
Wow, I can't believe it.

808
00:28:47,025 --> 00:28:48,158
Amazing.

809
00:28:48,159 --> 00:28:49,226
(A jaw-dropping stunt)

810
00:28:50,195 --> 00:28:54,598
(Snake coming out of the mouth)

811
00:28:55,467 --> 00:28:56,600
Wow.

812
00:28:57,035 --> 00:28:58,268
Did he eat the snake?

813
00:28:58,370 --> 00:28:59,437
Wait.

814
00:29:00,772 --> 00:29:02,372
It's like kissing.

815
00:29:02,373 --> 00:29:03,874
Oh my gosh.

816
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:06,410
I guess that snake isn't venomous.

817
00:29:06,513 --> 00:29:08,646
He could give Mr. Kim Byung-man
a run for his money.

818
00:29:08,647 --> 00:29:09,380
Right.

819
00:29:09,381 --> 00:29:11,049
The snake looks so harmless.

820
00:29:11,050 --> 00:29:12,050
It's kind of cute.

821
00:29:12,051 --> 00:29:13,351
What a derpy little noodle.

822
00:29:13,352 --> 00:29:16,688
The way it's hissing reminds me
of a chihuahua barking.

823
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:18,222
He's so small.

824
00:29:18,223 --> 00:29:19,056
Come on.

825
00:29:19,658 --> 00:29:20,591
Can I touch it?

826
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:23,127
(Slip)

827
00:29:23,128 --> 00:29:24,362
I want to touch it too.

828
00:29:24,363 --> 00:29:26,564
Don't tease me, okay?

829
00:29:27,299 --> 00:29:29,634
- "Don't tease me."
- Good snake.

830
00:29:29,635 --> 00:29:30,468
(Tremble)

831
00:29:30,469 --> 00:29:33,074
She's always so scared,
but she still wants to touch.

832
00:29:34,106 --> 00:29:34,973
(She's a brave scaredy cat.)

833
00:29:34,980 --> 00:29:36,580
Curiosity got the best of me.

834
00:29:38,277 --> 00:29:40,078
(Trying again)

835
00:29:40,612 --> 00:29:42,680
She got up the courage.

836
00:29:42,681 --> 00:29:43,847
(Frowning)

837
00:29:43,848 --> 00:29:44,782
(Jump)

838
00:29:45,317 --> 00:29:47,552
(Teasing the scaredy cat for fun)

839
00:29:47,553 --> 00:29:48,419
So cute.

840
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:51,055
- It's slippery. Touch it.
- Oh gosh!

841
00:29:51,390 --> 00:29:52,590
Slippery.

842
00:29:52,591 --> 00:29:53,992
(Too fun not to do it again.)

843
00:29:53,993 --> 00:29:55,360
Okay, let's get back to the jungle.

844
00:29:55,361 --> 00:29:57,462
Okay, back to the jungle.

845
00:29:57,463 --> 00:29:59,564
- Are you leaving?
- Goodbye!

846
00:29:59,565 --> 00:30:00,798
(Thanks for bearing with us.)

847
00:30:00,996 --> 00:30:02,265
This is so much fun.

848
00:30:02,499 --> 00:30:03,867
So fun.

849
00:30:04,768 --> 00:30:06,190
They keep coming down.

850
00:30:06,191 --> 00:30:07,904
There's one more.

851
00:30:08,778 --> 00:30:12,578
- I think they want to eat the fruit.
- Yeah.

852
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:14,564
Are we allowed to feed them?

853
00:30:14,565 --> 00:30:15,512
- No.
- Okay.

854
00:30:15,625 --> 00:30:17,147
It's just for people?

855
00:30:17,258 --> 00:30:18,281
Yes, for people only.

856
00:30:18,282 --> 00:30:19,948
Not for animals.

857
00:30:19,955 --> 00:30:21,596
(Feeding wildlife is strictly prohibited
to protect the ecosystem.)

858
00:30:21,776 --> 00:30:25,216
After we're done,
let's go to our campsite.

859
00:30:25,229 --> 00:30:26,789
It takes another two hours.

860
00:30:26,790 --> 00:30:28,922
- Two hours?
- You can finish the fruit first.

861
00:30:29,062 --> 00:30:30,293
Uphills and downhills.

862
00:30:30,382 --> 00:30:32,562
- After we finish eating?
- Yes.

863
00:30:32,742 --> 00:30:33,864
We've charged our energy!

864
00:30:34,531 --> 00:30:37,462
He says the uphills and downhills
come after this.

865
00:30:37,463 --> 00:30:39,088
- So eat up.
- Got it.

866
00:30:39,202 --> 00:30:41,304
Okay. Let's go to camp
after we finish this.

867
00:30:41,305 --> 00:30:42,139
Okay.

868
00:30:42,505 --> 00:30:43,874
Follow Ipu.

869
00:30:44,385 --> 00:30:45,742
We follow Ipu.

870
00:30:45,743 --> 00:30:50,080
Let's go together.

871
00:30:50,845 --> 00:30:52,398
(Indonesia)

872
00:30:53,018 --> 00:30:57,105
(They'll be traveling
for another two hours.)

873
00:30:57,958 --> 00:31:00,638
(Back on the trail with music)

874
00:31:00,731 --> 00:31:04,227
<i>- Abra-ca-Empty
- Abra-ca-Empty</i>

875
00:31:04,718 --> 00:31:07,478
(Can't have a jungle without this song!)

876
00:31:09,325 --> 00:31:11,325
<i>- Let it all go</i>
<i>- Let it all go</i>

877
00:31:11,364 --> 00:31:12,736
<i>- Get rid of it
- Get rid of it</i>

878
00:31:12,804 --> 00:31:14,838
<i>Get rid of it all!</i>

879
00:31:15,537 --> 00:31:17,537
We really got rid of it all today.

880
00:31:17,667 --> 00:31:18,642
- We really did.
- True.

881
00:31:18,643 --> 00:31:20,243
This song's a bop.

882
00:31:21,591 --> 00:31:24,881
This is where the real trek begins.

883
00:31:27,175 --> 00:31:29,519
The vines have turned into stairs.

884
00:31:30,220 --> 00:31:31,321
Vine stairs.

885
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:37,661
Talk about hitting the vine jackpot.

886
00:31:40,006 --> 00:31:44,634
Forget deep roots.
We've got the whole vine now.

887
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:47,737
We've come down a long way.

888
00:31:47,873 --> 00:31:48,805
Right?

889
00:31:49,372 --> 00:31:51,947
You can see some houses down there.

890
00:31:51,948 --> 00:31:52,909
It's a village.

891
00:31:52,937 --> 00:31:54,177
Ipu.

892
00:31:54,216 --> 00:31:55,512
Is that our camp?

893
00:31:56,050 --> 00:31:57,562
Not now.

894
00:31:57,563 --> 00:31:58,877
Two more hours to go.

895
00:31:58,963 --> 00:32:00,050
- Two hours?
- Two hours?

896
00:32:00,117 --> 00:32:01,551
- Another two hours?
- He says it's not here.

897
00:32:02,434 --> 00:32:04,574
Two hours of uphill and downhill.

898
00:32:04,575 --> 00:32:06,089
So it starts now.

899
00:32:06,161 --> 00:32:07,524
I guess we have to go up once.

900
00:32:08,334 --> 00:32:12,201
- Up and down.
- He says it keeps coming.

901
00:32:12,261 --> 00:32:14,097
<i>Up, down, up, up, down</i>

902
00:32:14,539 --> 00:32:17,206
(Singing their worries away)

903
00:32:17,439 --> 00:32:18,502
She's so funny.

904
00:32:19,069 --> 00:32:20,270
My kind of humor.

905
00:32:22,058 --> 00:32:24,508
I can hear something refreshing.

906
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:25,909
Huh?

907
00:32:26,370 --> 00:32:27,344
What?

908
00:32:28,812 --> 00:32:30,097
We're crossing over water?

909
00:32:30,098 --> 00:32:33,483
I don't see any way around the water.

910
00:32:33,704 --> 00:32:35,218
Ipu!

911
00:32:35,564 --> 00:32:37,430
- Do we have to go there?
- Yeah.

912
00:32:37,988 --> 00:32:39,789
Seriously?

913
00:32:39,790 --> 00:32:41,948
(A wild stream appears.)

914
00:32:42,441 --> 00:32:44,895
So this is why Ipu came barefoot.

915
00:32:45,428 --> 00:32:47,097
Do we have to take our shoes off?

916
00:32:47,864 --> 00:32:49,332
I think we're just going to get wet.

917
00:32:49,528 --> 00:32:50,800
We keep them on.

918
00:32:51,401 --> 00:32:53,401
I guess it's better than going barefoot.

919
00:32:54,075 --> 00:32:55,268
Be careful.

920
00:32:55,421 --> 00:32:56,873
Be careful.

921
00:32:58,208 --> 00:33:00,343
Wow, it's really steep.

922
00:33:00,461 --> 00:33:02,045
Careful, it's slippery.

923
00:33:02,512 --> 00:33:04,548
- Be careful, everyone!
- Okay.

924
00:33:04,549 --> 00:33:06,175
(Carefully)

925
00:33:06,481 --> 00:33:07,584
(Slippery)

926
00:33:07,585 --> 00:33:08,518
Watch your steps.

927
00:33:08,588 --> 00:33:11,154
Please keep a safe distance.

928
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:13,401
(Wet ground means
keeping your distance is a must.)

929
00:33:16,768 --> 00:33:20,363
It's like a refreshing little waterfall.

930
00:33:20,931 --> 00:33:22,332
It looks so refreshing!

931
00:33:22,832 --> 00:33:25,519
Wow, it really feels refreshing.

932
00:33:25,539 --> 00:33:26,959
- It's so different.
- I want to dip my feet in so bad.

933
00:33:27,837 --> 00:33:30,073
I'm going to wash my hands and my face.

934
00:33:30,144 --> 00:33:32,475
Wow, so cold!

935
00:33:35,497 --> 00:33:36,411
This feels so good.

936
00:33:36,657 --> 00:33:41,518
(Feels like the heat just melted away)

937
00:33:41,571 --> 00:33:42,852
Should I try dipping my feet in?

938
00:33:43,091 --> 00:33:44,087
Let's do it.

939
00:33:44,571 --> 00:33:45,989
Shall we?

940
00:33:46,808 --> 00:33:47,823
(Rolling up the pants)

941
00:33:47,824 --> 00:33:50,225
I think it'd be less slippery
with shoes on.

942
00:33:52,271 --> 00:33:54,230
Wow, it's so cold.

943
00:33:54,901 --> 00:33:57,000
- Did you just walk in?
- Yeah!

944
00:33:58,602 --> 00:34:00,103
It's so refreshing. I want to stay here.

945
00:34:00,401 --> 00:34:01,441
- Seriously.
- Really?

946
00:34:01,442 --> 00:34:03,127
I want to lie down here.

947
00:34:03,128 --> 00:34:04,040
Me too.

948
00:34:04,474 --> 00:34:07,010
Just letting go
and getting my shoes soaked...

949
00:34:07,611 --> 00:34:09,279
feels so damn good.

950
00:34:10,213 --> 00:34:11,314
I want to jump in.

951
00:34:11,315 --> 00:34:14,217
The water in my shoes...

952
00:34:15,452 --> 00:34:17,154
feels so weird.

953
00:34:17,155 --> 00:34:18,855
But I don't want to leave.

954
00:34:18,902 --> 00:34:21,458
Because leaving this place
is probably going to feel worse.

955
00:34:21,475 --> 00:34:23,475
I'm feeling exactly that right now.

956
00:34:23,602 --> 00:34:24,995
It feels pretty bad.

957
00:34:25,495 --> 00:34:27,381
But we're probably going to get
wet again, right?

958
00:34:27,382 --> 00:34:29,332
- Of course.
- Up and down.

959
00:34:29,462 --> 00:34:31,768
Just when our shoes start to dry,
it's downhill again.

960
00:34:31,909 --> 00:34:32,836
Alright.

961
00:34:32,895 --> 00:34:33,837
Let's go.

962
00:34:33,838 --> 00:34:36,298
Okay, let's go!

963
00:34:36,299 --> 00:34:38,466
(After a brief break, they keep going.)

964
00:34:39,195 --> 00:34:41,945
Shoes are a little slippery
now that they're wet.

965
00:34:41,946 --> 00:34:43,847
Be careful.

966
00:34:44,020 --> 00:34:45,749
It's pretty steep.

967
00:34:46,413 --> 00:34:47,617
Ugh.

968
00:34:48,067 --> 00:34:49,419
Darn.

969
00:34:49,719 --> 00:34:52,122
Gosh.

970
00:34:52,756 --> 00:34:55,025
Wait, is it all uphill from here?

971
00:34:56,084 --> 00:34:58,171
Up down.

972
00:34:58,418 --> 00:35:00,418
- Everyone okay?
- I'm okay.

973
00:35:00,419 --> 00:35:02,432
- Yes.
- Thank you.

974
00:35:03,039 --> 00:35:05,272
(Already two hours into the jungle trek)

975
00:35:06,092 --> 00:35:08,685
(Even Miss Sunshine is out of smiles.)

976
00:35:09,839 --> 00:35:12,243
Just a moment.

977
00:35:12,923 --> 00:35:15,311
We must be at least halfway there, right?

978
00:35:16,196 --> 00:35:18,179
Two more hours of up and down.

979
00:35:18,180 --> 00:35:19,243
Two more hours?

980
00:35:19,244 --> 00:35:21,451
- Why isn't the time reduced?
- Can we just sleep here?

981
00:35:21,961 --> 00:35:23,253
How's there still that much time left?

982
00:35:24,087 --> 00:35:26,322
An hour ago,
you said it'll take two hours.

983
00:35:26,328 --> 00:35:28,096
And now, you're telling us
there are two more hours.

984
00:35:28,097 --> 00:35:29,059
To make you happy.

985
00:35:29,168 --> 00:35:30,048
(Pause)

986
00:35:30,181 --> 00:35:32,181
Why do you keep saying...

987
00:35:32,201 --> 00:35:34,201
there are two hours left?

988
00:35:34,221 --> 00:35:36,221
I want to make you feel happy.

989
00:35:36,235 --> 00:35:38,301
- I'm not happy.
- "Two hours left."

990
00:35:39,369 --> 00:35:41,471
It's not even 40 minutes or something.

991
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,500
But 2 hours feels so far away.

992
00:35:43,573 --> 00:35:45,709
There's only so much false hope
we can take.

993
00:35:45,740 --> 00:35:47,740
This isn't false hope. It's just torture!

994
00:35:49,260 --> 00:35:51,884
Can you smell it?

995
00:35:52,148 --> 00:35:54,818
He's really good at distracting us.

996
00:35:54,838 --> 00:35:55,838
Do you see that mountain?

997
00:35:56,484 --> 00:35:58,704
Two more hours of up and down
until we reach there.

998
00:35:58,811 --> 00:36:01,898
- That mountain?
- Yeah.

999
00:36:02,204 --> 00:36:05,091
Two more hours of up and down.

1000
00:36:05,258 --> 00:36:07,391
I don't like that.

1001
00:36:07,404 --> 00:36:08,504
- Why?
- Why?

1002
00:36:08,684 --> 00:36:10,366
Who could do it?

1003
00:36:10,431 --> 00:36:12,068
- You.
- Me?

1004
00:36:12,797 --> 00:36:13,737
Let me see.

1005
00:36:13,765 --> 00:36:15,638
Can you sleep in the jungle?

1006
00:36:15,939 --> 00:36:17,774
"Let me see."

1007
00:36:17,958 --> 00:36:19,676
"Let me see," she says.

1008
00:36:20,258 --> 00:36:22,505
Let's go with orangutans.

1009
00:36:22,605 --> 00:36:25,348
Okay, with orangutans!

1010
00:36:25,676 --> 00:36:27,049
With orangutans!

1011
00:36:27,050 --> 00:36:28,409
With orangutans,

1012
00:36:28,410 --> 00:36:30,487
we can do everything!

1013
00:36:30,976 --> 00:36:36,860
- With orangutans!
- Yeah, let's go!

1014
00:36:37,007 --> 00:36:39,429
I love the energy.

1015
00:36:39,894 --> 00:36:40,864
This is crazy.

1016
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,381
(After all that uphill...)

1017
00:36:44,354 --> 00:36:49,805
(Now it's endless downhill.)

1018
00:36:51,585 --> 00:36:55,512
(30 minutes into the downhill course)

1019
00:36:55,805 --> 00:36:57,805
- Are you okay?
- Yes!

1020
00:36:57,963 --> 00:37:00,016
- It's okay. I'm okay.
- Is number 1 okay?

1021
00:37:00,176 --> 00:37:02,285
Number 1 is not okay.

1022
00:37:02,852 --> 00:37:04,462
- Is number 2 okay?
- Number 3, no.

1023
00:37:04,463 --> 00:37:06,489
Number 2 is okay!

1024
00:37:06,856 --> 00:37:08,947
Alright, even numbers!

1025
00:37:08,948 --> 00:37:11,981
Odd and even!

1026
00:37:12,174 --> 00:37:14,664
Odd numbers are not okay,
even numbers are okay.

1027
00:37:15,314 --> 00:37:16,754
I can call for a helicopter later.

1028
00:37:16,788 --> 00:37:18,201
- Huh?
- A helicopter.

1029
00:37:18,234 --> 00:37:19,335
An elephant?

1030
00:37:19,336 --> 00:37:20,203
Helicopter!

1031
00:37:20,204 --> 00:37:21,437
- Helicopter.
- An elephant?

1032
00:37:21,496 --> 00:37:23,306
Helicopter!

1033
00:37:23,336 --> 00:37:24,607
Chuff!

1034
00:37:25,029 --> 00:37:26,342
She's gone mad.

1035
00:37:26,343 --> 00:37:28,211
The heat's gotten into her.

1036
00:37:28,212 --> 00:37:29,679
Good lord.

1037
00:37:31,519 --> 00:37:32,615
She's gone crazy!

1038
00:37:32,616 --> 00:37:34,105
(Random bursts of high energy)

1039
00:37:36,865 --> 00:37:37,821
Ipu.

1040
00:37:37,898 --> 00:37:39,238
- Are you tired?
- No.

1041
00:37:39,271 --> 00:37:40,931
- But you look tired.
- No.

1042
00:37:41,958 --> 00:37:43,259
- You look tired.
- I saw that.

1043
00:37:45,411 --> 00:37:46,744
(You definitely sighed just now.)

1044
00:37:47,183 --> 00:37:48,436
- Tired.
- You?

1045
00:37:48,537 --> 00:37:49,666
- You.
- Not me.

1046
00:37:49,667 --> 00:37:50,500
Not me, he says.

1047
00:37:50,623 --> 00:37:51,634
Okay.

1048
00:37:51,968 --> 00:37:53,636
Let me see.

1049
00:37:54,237 --> 00:37:55,371
Ipu.

1050
00:37:55,705 --> 00:37:57,140
Does the campsite...

1051
00:37:57,450 --> 00:37:58,775
have snakes there?

1052
00:37:59,303 --> 00:38:01,090
- Snakes at the campsite?
- Yes, snakes.

1053
00:38:01,417 --> 00:38:02,846
Only crocodiles.

1054
00:38:02,910 --> 00:38:04,447
Only crocodiles?

1055
00:38:04,448 --> 00:38:05,548
Crocodiles?

1056
00:38:05,630 --> 00:38:06,883
What about tigers?

1057
00:38:07,190 --> 00:38:08,351
Tigers are already gone.

1058
00:38:08,352 --> 00:38:09,853
Already gone? Where to?

1059
00:38:10,445 --> 00:38:11,387
Where did they go?

1060
00:38:12,345 --> 00:38:14,639
(Ipu picks something up
instead of answering.)

1061
00:38:14,665 --> 00:38:16,926
Ipu, what's that?

1062
00:38:17,171 --> 00:38:18,228
Fruit.

1063
00:38:18,272 --> 00:38:19,305
- Fruit?
- Yes.

1064
00:38:20,697 --> 00:38:22,131
That's what gets me. So funny.

1065
00:38:22,179 --> 00:38:24,534
He can't be bothered to answer.

1066
00:38:24,579 --> 00:38:25,401
He's tired.

1067
00:38:25,439 --> 00:38:27,470
- Are you tired?
- No.

1068
00:38:27,552 --> 00:38:28,605
No?

1069
00:38:28,972 --> 00:38:30,206
What fruit is it?

1070
00:38:30,785 --> 00:38:32,405
(Endless questions)

1071
00:38:34,085 --> 00:38:36,179
He danced instead of answering me.

1072
00:38:36,339 --> 00:38:38,780
- He seems tired.
- Very.

1073
00:38:39,582 --> 00:38:41,918
We have two hours left.

1074
00:38:42,485 --> 00:38:43,994
You've got this, right?

1075
00:38:43,995 --> 00:38:45,154
You've got this.

1076
00:38:45,315 --> 00:38:46,623
He's so funny.

1077
00:38:49,168 --> 00:38:50,688
There's water.

1078
00:38:51,021 --> 00:38:52,362
Wow, a creek!

1079
00:38:53,895 --> 00:38:55,732
Our shower place!

1080
00:38:55,733 --> 00:38:59,287
(A river appears beyond the dense jungle.)

1081
00:39:00,387 --> 00:39:03,667
(The current looks pretty strong.)

1082
00:39:04,033 --> 00:39:05,726
You can swim here.

1083
00:39:05,747 --> 00:39:06,743
- What did you say?
- What?

1084
00:39:06,820 --> 00:39:08,878
We're crossing the river?

1085
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:11,014
- Yes.
- Wow, okay.

1086
00:39:11,881 --> 00:39:13,917
We just jump in there?

1087
00:39:13,994 --> 00:39:16,719
The current's pretty strong here.

1088
00:39:16,894 --> 00:39:17,720
Liar!

1089
00:39:17,908 --> 00:39:19,286
You're a liar.

1090
00:39:19,287 --> 00:39:20,590
(They have to wade across
to the other side.)

1091
00:39:20,921 --> 00:39:23,615
(Unexpected underwater trekking)

1092
00:39:23,828 --> 00:39:26,696
How are we going to cross over
with all our stuff?

1093
00:39:27,597 --> 00:39:29,332
It looks pretty deep.

1094
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:32,302
I think it comes up to your thighs.

1095
00:39:32,361 --> 00:39:34,361
Still, what do we do?

1096
00:39:34,693 --> 00:39:38,039
(For safety, the crew crosses first.)

1097
00:39:38,259 --> 00:39:40,677
They're linking arms
so they don't get swept away.

1098
00:39:42,019 --> 00:39:43,066
(Watching makes them even more nervous.)

1099
00:39:43,099 --> 00:39:45,014
Our buddies crossing the river.

1100
00:39:45,615 --> 00:39:48,618
I'm gonna get soaked anyway,
so I might as well roll it down.

1101
00:39:49,764 --> 00:39:51,354
He says it's going to be
slippery barefoot.

1102
00:39:51,444 --> 00:39:52,355
I'll be fine.

1103
00:39:52,356 --> 00:39:53,790
- You sure?
- Yeah, I'll try.

1104
00:39:54,104 --> 00:39:55,391
Okay.

1105
00:39:56,125 --> 00:39:57,860
We'll be grabbing this.

1106
00:39:58,461 --> 00:40:00,897
Okay, let's go!

1107
00:40:01,766 --> 00:40:05,702
(Won Ji carefully takes her first step.)

1108
00:40:07,205 --> 00:40:08,839
- It's cold.
- It's refreshing.

1109
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:10,340
Ipu, you're too fast.

1110
00:40:10,875 --> 00:40:12,375
Ipu, you're too fast.

1111
00:40:13,678 --> 00:40:14,845
Ipu is too fast.

1112
00:40:17,816 --> 00:40:19,517
The current is really strong,

1113
00:40:19,518 --> 00:40:21,352
so we have to walk diagonally.

1114
00:40:22,621 --> 00:40:24,544
The current is really strong.

1115
00:40:24,777 --> 00:40:26,300
It doesn't look like it, though.

1116
00:40:26,324 --> 00:40:28,925
(She staggers if she lets her guard down.)

1117
00:40:29,227 --> 00:40:32,430
(The younger ones
slowly enter the water too.)

1118
00:40:35,166 --> 00:40:36,166
(Harimu is the only one taking it easy.)

1119
00:40:36,167 --> 00:40:37,367
It's slippery.

1120
00:40:40,038 --> 00:40:41,604
The current is really strong.

1121
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:43,774
The current is insane.

1122
00:40:44,843 --> 00:40:46,144
(Especially hard for a paper doll,
who lacks balance)

1123
00:40:46,145 --> 00:40:47,478
I can't keep my balance.

1124
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:54,384
(She bravely pushes
through the strong current.)

1125
00:40:54,520 --> 00:40:56,486
This is fun.

1126
00:40:57,021 --> 00:40:59,422
(The eldest gains
confidence and speeds up.)

1127
00:41:00,425 --> 00:41:02,092
(Gabee and Harimu slow down
for the frightened Sian.)

1128
00:41:02,093 --> 00:41:03,427
She's already way over there.

1129
00:41:03,828 --> 00:41:05,929
I made it. Thank you, Ipu.

1130
00:41:06,764 --> 00:41:07,764
It's so cool.

1131
00:41:09,298 --> 00:41:10,540
This is so refreshing.

1132
00:41:10,564 --> 00:41:12,502
(The younger ones are almost there too.)

1133
00:41:13,601 --> 00:41:18,342
(They safely crossed the river.)

1134
00:41:18,610 --> 00:41:19,743
We're eating here.

1135
00:41:20,278 --> 00:41:22,179
- Let's go eat.
- I'm exhausted.

1136
00:41:23,783 --> 00:41:25,916
- Harimu, do you want to get in the water?
- Yes.

1137
00:41:25,917 --> 00:41:27,184
Should we just soak our feet?

1138
00:41:27,185 --> 00:41:29,086
I wanna take this off and get in.

1139
00:41:31,823 --> 00:41:32,890
(Staggering)

1140
00:41:33,659 --> 00:41:35,092
This is like dancing too.

1141
00:41:35,960 --> 00:41:37,394
(She turns her fall into a scorpion pose.)

1142
00:41:37,395 --> 00:41:38,462
I'm dying.

1143
00:41:39,030 --> 00:41:39,997
It's so refreshing.

1144
00:41:40,431 --> 00:41:42,665
- I just want to stay here.
- Me too.

1145
00:41:42,800 --> 00:41:43,967
It's so cool.

1146
00:41:43,968 --> 00:41:45,301
(Looking around)

1147
00:41:45,302 --> 00:41:47,137
Ipu, what are you looking for?

1148
00:41:47,305 --> 00:41:48,171
A stone.

1149
00:41:48,773 --> 00:41:50,107
Another new thing.

1150
00:41:50,843 --> 00:41:52,175
He's doing something fun again.

1151
00:41:52,744 --> 00:41:54,044
I think this is mud.

1152
00:41:54,912 --> 00:41:56,813
(Ipu shows off a new trick.)

1153
00:41:57,116 --> 00:41:59,149
It really rubs off on his hand.

1154
00:41:59,150 --> 00:42:00,450
(A clay-like stone that turns into mud)

1155
00:42:01,119 --> 00:42:02,352
That's amazing.

1156
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:04,021
It's totally like a crayon.

1157
00:42:04,989 --> 00:42:05,822
What is this?

1158
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:06,990
A stone.

1159
00:42:07,392 --> 00:42:08,224
A stone?

1160
00:42:09,060 --> 00:42:11,137
(It is a stone, though.)

1161
00:42:11,162 --> 00:42:12,028
- A stone?
- Yes.

1162
00:42:12,029 --> 00:42:14,164
The color is so vivid.

1163
00:42:14,732 --> 00:42:16,466
(Smoothing)

1164
00:42:16,801 --> 00:42:18,235
(Ipu paints Gabee's face.)

1165
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:22,105
(He starts decorating Gabee.)

1166
00:42:23,074 --> 00:42:26,376
(With careful touches)

1167
00:42:28,313 --> 00:42:29,945
Looks like he's just playing around.

1168
00:42:31,616 --> 00:42:33,817
(Laughing)

1169
00:42:34,152 --> 00:42:35,486
I think it's done.

1170
00:42:37,755 --> 00:42:40,824
(He even pays attention to the symmetry.)

1171
00:42:41,459 --> 00:42:42,893
Ipu did this for me.

1172
00:42:44,965 --> 00:42:46,497
(Like a fierce cat)

1173
00:42:48,266 --> 00:42:50,300
(The artist proudly admires his work.)

1174
00:42:50,735 --> 00:42:52,202
(Glancing)

1175
00:42:52,470 --> 00:42:53,336
Come here, Ipu.

1176
00:42:54,138 --> 00:42:57,107
I can write your name in Korean.
Do you want to see?

1177
00:42:58,409 --> 00:43:01,177
(Deeply focused)

1178
00:43:01,546 --> 00:43:04,548
(She carefully writes his name.)

1179
00:43:05,283 --> 00:43:06,717
- This is your name.
- Thank you.

1180
00:43:07,185 --> 00:43:08,719
Done. I like it.

1181
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:10,120
I wrote his name on his arm.

1182
00:43:10,356 --> 00:43:11,522
That's so sweet.

1183
00:43:11,523 --> 00:43:12,723
(It's pretty, so it's fine.)

1184
00:43:12,890 --> 00:43:13,756
This might work.

1185
00:43:13,757 --> 00:43:15,725
Let's try writing Abra-ca-Empty with it.

1186
00:43:15,726 --> 00:43:16,626
"Empty."

1187
00:43:16,627 --> 00:43:18,094
(Swiping)

1188
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:21,707
(She leaves a semi-permanent memory.)

1189
00:43:21,732 --> 00:43:22,599
This is our mark.

1190
00:43:23,468 --> 00:43:25,269
You've decorated diaries before, right?

1191
00:43:25,270 --> 00:43:26,270
Of course I have.

1192
00:43:29,474 --> 00:43:30,274
Hello.

1193
00:43:31,342 --> 00:43:32,942
Here's your lunch.

1194
00:43:32,943 --> 00:43:35,746
(Lunch is finally ready.)

1195
00:43:35,880 --> 00:43:38,114
- What's that?
- This looks so nice.

1196
00:43:39,217 --> 00:43:41,718
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

1197
00:43:41,743 --> 00:43:44,922
(Lunch is nasi goreng
topped with chicken.)

1198
00:43:45,524 --> 00:43:47,357
This is amazing.

1199
00:43:48,693 --> 00:43:49,860
Chicken.

1200
00:43:50,561 --> 00:43:53,463
(Pretty much means "thank you so much.")

1201
00:43:53,998 --> 00:43:56,533
Eating with our feet
in the water would be amazing.

1202
00:43:56,534 --> 00:43:58,134
I'd be so happy.

1203
00:43:59,604 --> 00:44:01,372
Should I sit here?

1204
00:44:01,373 --> 00:44:02,839
(She finds a suitable rock and sits.)

1205
00:44:03,307 --> 00:44:06,075
(They take a bite
as soon as they sit down.)

1206
00:44:08,546 --> 00:44:10,246
It's spicy and so good.

1207
00:44:11,082 --> 00:44:12,282
Is this nasi goreng?

1208
00:44:13,351 --> 00:44:14,718
Yes, I think so.

1209
00:44:16,020 --> 00:44:18,288
(Now, a bite of chicken)

1210
00:44:18,623 --> 00:44:20,156
The chicken is good.

1211
00:44:20,157 --> 00:44:21,124
Exactly.

1212
00:44:22,794 --> 00:44:24,361
(Excited)

1213
00:44:24,362 --> 00:44:25,329
I love this.

1214
00:44:26,597 --> 00:44:27,430
Beer.

1215
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:30,133
Beer.

1216
00:44:30,134 --> 00:44:31,601
(The vibe makes you crave a beer.)

1217
00:44:31,602 --> 00:44:32,402
A bottle of beer.

1218
00:44:36,941 --> 00:44:39,576
There's nothing Ipu can't do.

1219
00:44:40,845 --> 00:44:42,145
He's using a piece of plastic.

1220
00:44:42,146 --> 00:44:44,080
(Making bird sounds
with a piece of plastic)

1221
00:44:45,383 --> 00:44:46,416
The sound is cute.

1222
00:44:46,417 --> 00:44:48,084
(He plays birdsong
using a piece of plastic.)

1223
00:44:48,753 --> 00:44:51,421
(They savor the chicken,
listening to artificial bird sounds.)

1224
00:44:51,789 --> 00:44:52,822
It's so delicious.

1225
00:44:52,823 --> 00:44:54,958
(Ipu wanders off somewhere again.)

1226
00:44:55,226 --> 00:44:57,327
Look at Ipu's nails.

1227
00:44:58,129 --> 00:44:59,597
He puts fake nails on his fingers.

1228
00:44:59,598 --> 00:45:01,465
- Oh, right.
- Look at that.

1229
00:45:02,100 --> 00:45:03,033
Is that real?

1230
00:45:03,434 --> 00:45:05,168
(He returns with nail extensions.)

1231
00:45:05,169 --> 00:45:07,737
- It's crazy.
- Ipu is a local here.

1232
00:45:08,773 --> 00:45:10,373
Harimu, bring it on.

1233
00:45:11,075 --> 00:45:12,709
- Harimu, bring it on.
- Why are they so long?

1234
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:13,877
I'm seriously jealous.

1235
00:45:14,278 --> 00:45:16,179
(Ipu's nails become communal property.)

1236
00:45:18,282 --> 00:45:19,682
It's stealing our food.

1237
00:45:20,852 --> 00:45:21,752
Hey.

1238
00:45:22,186 --> 00:45:23,887
(The monkey eats and runs.)

1239
00:45:24,188 --> 00:45:25,321
It eats behind us.

1240
00:45:25,953 --> 00:45:27,192
(It snatches their food in an instant.)

1241
00:45:27,193 --> 00:45:28,158
It's cute.

1242
00:45:28,893 --> 00:45:30,660
- Amazing.
- It's eating in such a hurry.

1243
00:45:31,195 --> 00:45:32,927
They're having the time of their lives.

1244
00:45:32,928 --> 00:45:34,197
(Almost like a company dinner)

1245
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:35,832
Monkey.

1246
00:45:35,833 --> 00:45:37,767
What are you doing? Come here.

1247
00:45:38,503 --> 00:45:40,737
(A quick monkey playtime)

1248
00:45:40,872 --> 00:45:42,372
(She plays well.)

1249
00:45:42,707 --> 00:45:44,641
Hold on.

1250
00:45:45,209 --> 00:45:46,809
Look over there.

1251
00:45:46,878 --> 00:45:49,078
(A new creature appears.)

1252
00:45:49,079 --> 00:45:49,946
A lizard?

1253
00:45:50,681 --> 00:45:53,650
- There really is a crocodile.
- It's huge.

1254
00:45:53,651 --> 00:45:55,051
It's not a crocodile, is it?

1255
00:45:55,052 --> 00:45:56,052
It's a lizard.

1256
00:45:56,053 --> 00:45:59,155
Its tongue is completely black.

1257
00:45:59,790 --> 00:46:01,324
I'm a huge fan of those.

1258
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:04,160
It's eyeing Ipu's bag.

1259
00:46:05,129 --> 00:46:07,230
(It shows interest in Ipu's bag.)

1260
00:46:07,231 --> 00:46:08,197
No, stop.

1261
00:46:08,333 --> 00:46:10,100
Ipu's eyes have changed again.

1262
00:46:10,101 --> 00:46:11,634
(The bag owner's gaze
suddenly turns fierce.)

1263
00:46:12,854 --> 00:46:14,203
Is he hunting?

1264
00:46:15,573 --> 00:46:16,673
This is true nature.

1265
00:46:16,674 --> 00:46:17,807
(A standoff over the bag)

1266
00:46:18,309 --> 00:46:19,175
Amazing.

1267
00:46:19,176 --> 00:46:20,110
(Sneaking closer)

1268
00:46:20,111 --> 00:46:22,112
(Threatening)

1269
00:46:22,680 --> 00:46:24,180
(Flinches)

1270
00:46:24,181 --> 00:46:25,415
They're exactly alike.

1271
00:46:26,150 --> 00:46:27,782
I think Ipu's trying to catch it.

1272
00:46:28,986 --> 00:46:31,321
This is an incredibly tense standoff.

1273
00:46:31,756 --> 00:46:32,923
Between Ipu...

1274
00:46:33,257 --> 00:46:34,958
(Thrilling)

1275
00:46:35,493 --> 00:46:36,560
And the lizard.

1276
00:46:36,561 --> 00:46:37,594
(He approaches at its eye level.)

1277
00:46:37,595 --> 00:46:39,062
I think he's going to catch it.

1278
00:46:39,063 --> 00:46:39,796
(Dashing)

1279
00:46:40,198 --> 00:46:42,365
(The water monitor briefly retreats.)

1280
00:46:42,867 --> 00:46:44,401
(He chases it fiercely.)

1281
00:46:44,702 --> 00:46:45,869
(Is it retreating for good?)

1282
00:46:45,870 --> 00:46:46,670
(Swishes around)

1283
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:51,708
(Chaos)

1284
00:46:52,310 --> 00:46:54,611
(It charges straight
at the two biggest scaredy-cats.)

1285
00:46:55,379 --> 00:46:58,182
(It makes a beeline for the river.)

1286
00:46:58,183 --> 00:46:59,249
It's amazing.

1287
00:46:59,584 --> 00:47:00,717
It's insane.

1288
00:47:02,186 --> 00:47:03,520
(An undignified exit)

1289
00:47:03,521 --> 00:47:05,153
It's funny how it
suddenly started swimming.

1290
00:47:06,357 --> 00:47:07,324
Pure nature.

1291
00:47:09,093 --> 00:47:12,896
I'd get to see a real lizard
in the wild for the first time.

1292
00:47:13,297 --> 00:47:15,498
It'd be so scary if they came out
while we're sleeping.

1293
00:47:15,499 --> 00:47:17,400
- Oh, no.
- They might come out at night.

1294
00:47:17,435 --> 00:47:18,969
I should hug my bag while I sleep.

1295
00:47:19,103 --> 00:47:21,237
I won't be able to sleep tonight.

1296
00:47:21,439 --> 00:47:22,239
Okay.

1297
00:47:22,506 --> 00:47:23,873
We're heading to the campsite now.

1298
00:47:24,108 --> 00:47:26,342
- Okay.
- Finally.

1299
00:47:26,410 --> 00:47:27,176
It takes two hours.

1300
00:47:27,177 --> 00:47:28,711
- Don't lie.
- Don't lie.

1301
00:47:28,712 --> 00:47:30,646
(The cry-wolf uncle
keeps going without a care.)

1302
00:47:30,647 --> 00:47:31,647
Okay, let's go.

1303
00:47:31,648 --> 00:47:32,448
- Okay.
- Let's go.

1304
00:47:32,449 --> 00:47:34,217
Let's see.

1305
00:47:34,485 --> 00:47:37,153
Let's see if it really takes two hours.

1306
00:47:37,422 --> 00:47:39,722
So far, we've been in the mountains.

1307
00:47:40,558 --> 00:47:43,260
Now it's starting to feel like a jungle.

1308
00:47:45,329 --> 00:47:47,664
There are so many more weeds.

1309
00:47:48,399 --> 00:47:50,567
It's getting more and more jungle-like.

1310
00:47:50,568 --> 00:47:51,768
It really feels like a jungle.

1311
00:47:52,203 --> 00:47:55,005
There seem to be lots of plants
you'd find in a jungle.

1312
00:47:55,009 --> 00:47:55,935
Right.

1313
00:47:56,707 --> 00:47:59,642
It looks like nature is
really well preserved here.

1314
00:47:59,978 --> 00:48:01,411
- I love it.
- I love it too.

1315
00:48:02,481 --> 00:48:06,183
It's much denser,
and the path has gotten really narrow.

1316
00:48:08,619 --> 00:48:11,387
I feel like I've come to a new planet.

1317
00:48:12,290 --> 00:48:13,423
It's awesome.

1318
00:48:13,424 --> 00:48:16,760
(Deeper and deeper into the jungle)

1319
00:48:17,261 --> 00:48:19,227
What are we doing
when we get to the campsite?

1320
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:21,698
- Ipu.
- Yes.

1321
00:48:21,932 --> 00:48:22,932
Do we have a schedule?

1322
00:48:23,434 --> 00:48:24,833
- Nothing.
- Nothing?

1323
00:48:25,336 --> 00:48:26,536
Nothing today.

1324
00:48:26,537 --> 00:48:27,904
(Yay, free time)

1325
00:48:28,039 --> 00:48:29,973
Nice. Let's swim and play.

1326
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:32,642
We definitely have to swim here.

1327
00:48:33,744 --> 00:48:35,511
(He spots something.)

1328
00:48:36,146 --> 00:48:38,554
What's that?

1329
00:48:38,894 --> 00:48:40,083
Is that the nail?

1330
00:48:40,084 --> 00:48:41,317
(Those nails from the stream)

1331
00:48:41,485 --> 00:48:42,985
Harimu, are you nervous?

1332
00:48:44,121 --> 00:48:45,354
- No.
- Are you?

1333
00:48:45,690 --> 00:48:46,456
No.

1334
00:48:47,224 --> 00:48:50,193
They look like they're
five times longer than your nails.

1335
00:48:50,328 --> 00:48:51,328
I know.

1336
00:48:51,329 --> 00:48:52,963
Isn't he making them too long?

1337
00:48:52,964 --> 00:48:55,565
I've never seen anyone
with longer nails than yours.

1338
00:48:55,566 --> 00:48:57,000
Natural nails.

1339
00:48:57,001 --> 00:48:59,002
(A slight sense of danger)

1340
00:48:59,136 --> 00:49:00,770
He's making them way too long.

1341
00:49:01,439 --> 00:49:02,439
(Challenge)

1342
00:49:02,907 --> 00:49:03,940
(How dare you.)

1343
00:49:06,177 --> 00:49:07,244
(Staggering)

1344
00:49:07,311 --> 00:49:08,445
(Queen Ipu's legs give out.)

1345
00:49:08,446 --> 00:49:09,212
Sorry.

1346
00:49:10,681 --> 00:49:13,116
- Oh, my.
- He's so charming.

1347
00:49:13,617 --> 00:49:14,784
Ipu is so charming.

1348
00:49:14,785 --> 00:49:16,052
(Ipu is acting cute.)

1349
00:49:16,253 --> 00:49:17,987
You're so funny.

1350
00:49:18,189 --> 00:49:19,256
You're very funny.

1351
00:49:19,257 --> 00:49:21,158
But it's so fun that everything here is...

1352
00:49:21,425 --> 00:49:23,693
basically his toy and his playground.

1353
00:49:23,694 --> 00:49:25,595
Exactly. That's so Ipu.

1354
00:49:27,398 --> 00:49:29,466
There's an even more
amazing spot over there.

1355
00:49:31,035 --> 00:49:32,902
There's someone over there too.

1356
00:49:33,871 --> 00:49:35,571
We're not crossing over there, are we?

1357
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:37,740
Is that our campsite?

1358
00:49:38,776 --> 00:49:41,177
Is that our campsite?

1359
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:42,712
Yes, that's it.

1360
00:49:43,314 --> 00:49:44,415
- Over there.
- Really?

1361
00:49:45,282 --> 00:49:47,717
(The campsite is across the stream.)

1362
00:49:47,718 --> 00:49:49,252
(Their second crossing already)

1363
00:49:49,887 --> 00:49:51,454
We're going.

1364
00:49:51,856 --> 00:49:52,756
It's refreshing.

1365
00:49:53,524 --> 00:49:55,358
This looks like it'll be the deepest one.

1366
00:49:56,327 --> 00:49:59,062
It's deep.

1367
00:49:59,636 --> 00:50:01,636
The current is really strong.

1368
00:50:05,168 --> 00:50:06,003
It's nice.

1369
00:50:06,201 --> 00:50:07,471
It's a funny life.

1370
00:50:07,634 --> 00:50:08,873
It's a very good life.

1371
00:50:10,088 --> 00:50:11,141
It's refreshing.

1372
00:50:13,586 --> 00:50:14,778
Are you all right?

1373
00:50:14,872 --> 00:50:15,779
Yes.

1374
00:50:15,926 --> 00:50:17,448
I'm so all right.

1375
00:50:19,362 --> 00:50:21,661
- Nice.
- It's refreshing.

1376
00:50:21,686 --> 00:50:24,517
(The cool water washes away all the heat.)

1377
00:50:27,903 --> 00:50:28,926
Thank you.

1378
00:50:28,963 --> 00:50:31,595
Thank you, Ipu.

1379
00:50:31,617 --> 00:50:32,663
(Ipu, thanks.)

1380
00:50:33,163 --> 00:50:35,163
(They finally crossed the river.)

1381
00:50:35,164 --> 00:50:37,416
It's so nice.

1382
00:50:37,577 --> 00:50:39,203
They're swimming over there.

1383
00:50:39,937 --> 00:50:41,305
Let's swim later too.

1384
00:50:41,510 --> 00:50:43,107
Here?

1385
00:50:43,817 --> 00:50:45,609
Is that our campsite?

1386
00:50:45,784 --> 00:50:47,784
You said we had two more hours to go.
You're a liar.

1387
00:50:48,064 --> 00:50:49,413
- Two minutes.
- Two minutes.

1388
00:50:49,414 --> 00:50:51,615
- Yes!
- Finally, only two minutes.

1389
00:50:51,924 --> 00:50:54,418
- Jungle!
- Welcome to the Jungle.

1390
00:50:54,419 --> 00:50:56,499
(As soon as we walk in,
they see an old, rundown hut.)

1391
00:50:57,199 --> 00:50:58,422
No way. Wait.

1392
00:50:58,923 --> 00:51:00,057
Hold on.

1393
00:51:01,358 --> 00:51:03,827
- I can't believe it.
- Those are bamboo houses.

1394
00:51:04,618 --> 00:51:06,830
Please. This is a lie.

1395
00:51:06,831 --> 00:51:07,811
(Flustered)

1396
00:51:07,971 --> 00:51:10,245
(Staggering)

1397
00:51:10,278 --> 00:51:12,970
How do people even find a place like this?

1398
00:51:14,438 --> 00:51:16,040
Seriously, this is legendary.

1399
00:51:16,041 --> 00:51:17,251
(Today's lodging is Eco-friendly.)

1400
00:51:18,157 --> 00:51:21,957
(About a four-hour trek to get here)

1401
00:51:22,313 --> 00:51:24,982
This is pretty much
an indigenous experience.

1402
00:51:26,383 --> 00:51:29,086
I should've brought just one outfit.

1403
00:51:29,087 --> 00:51:33,850
(It took them eight hours
to get here from Medan.)

1404
00:51:33,917 --> 00:51:36,460
It's just divided into different spaces.

1405
00:51:36,461 --> 00:51:38,796
It's really well built with bamboo.

1406
00:51:38,894 --> 00:51:41,398
It's totally a bamboo house.

1407
00:51:42,001 --> 00:51:43,561
What is that?

1408
00:51:44,441 --> 00:51:48,294
(Orangutans show up here all the time.)

1409
00:51:48,420 --> 00:51:54,014
(This jungle lodge coexists
with the wildlife.)

1410
00:51:54,420 --> 00:51:57,681
There are so many houses here.

1411
00:51:58,531 --> 00:52:00,050
Where's our home?

1412
00:52:02,373 --> 00:52:04,021
- The blue one.
- The blue one.

1413
00:52:04,521 --> 00:52:05,656
That must be it.

1414
00:52:06,123 --> 00:52:07,191
Let's go.

1415
00:52:08,092 --> 00:52:09,426
Let's check it out.

1416
00:52:09,952 --> 00:52:11,261
This is it.

1417
00:52:13,085 --> 00:52:14,198
This is your room.

1418
00:52:16,145 --> 00:52:18,425
(Arriving at their lodging
eight hours after leaving their hotel)

1419
00:52:18,426 --> 00:52:19,470
A room tour.

1420
00:52:20,032 --> 00:52:20,871
What?

1421
00:52:22,758 --> 00:52:24,441
That's unbelievable.

1422
00:52:25,943 --> 00:52:27,411
- How can it be like this?
- Gosh.

1423
00:52:28,512 --> 00:52:30,166
I've never slept in a place like this.

1424
00:52:30,200 --> 00:52:31,348
How is this possible?

1425
00:52:32,607 --> 00:52:35,467
(Here's today's lodging.)

1426
00:52:37,107 --> 00:52:40,245
(You can see the entire interior
at a glance.)

1427
00:52:41,391 --> 00:52:44,085
(An ultra-minimalist lodge)

1428
00:52:44,145 --> 00:52:45,429
There's our backpack!

1429
00:52:45,605 --> 00:52:47,398
Our backpack is here.

1430
00:52:48,304 --> 00:52:49,199
This is insane.

1431
00:52:49,200 --> 00:52:51,535
Let us take a look around our room.

1432
00:52:51,565 --> 00:52:52,536
A room tour.

1433
00:52:52,891 --> 00:52:54,338
Room One.

1434
00:52:54,339 --> 00:52:55,806
Room Two.

1435
00:52:56,672 --> 00:52:58,142
Room Three.

1436
00:52:58,742 --> 00:53:00,244
Room Four.

1437
00:53:00,986 --> 00:53:02,812
And...

1438
00:53:03,047 --> 00:53:04,948
there are no windows.

1439
00:53:04,949 --> 00:53:06,593
(This room feels insanely open.)

1440
00:53:06,773 --> 00:53:08,773
The mosquito net has a hole in it.

1441
00:53:09,207 --> 00:53:11,340
(Stunned)

1442
00:53:11,820 --> 00:53:13,053
- Do you like it?
- It's good!

1443
00:53:13,054 --> 00:53:15,125
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1444
00:53:15,308 --> 00:53:16,661
There's no electricity.

1445
00:53:16,714 --> 00:53:18,714
- No electricity?
- No.

1446
00:53:19,229 --> 00:53:20,464
- No lights either?
- Yes.

1447
00:53:20,528 --> 00:53:21,732
Okay.

1448
00:53:22,360 --> 00:53:23,733
- You're right.
- There's nothing here.

1449
00:53:23,734 --> 00:53:24,794
You don't get a signal here either.

1450
00:53:24,795 --> 00:53:26,795
We should rely on our video light.

1451
00:53:27,487 --> 00:53:30,694
If you want to make a call,
climb up a tree.

1452
00:53:30,695 --> 00:53:31,807
Okay.

1453
00:53:32,810 --> 00:53:34,978
If we get bored, let's climb a tree.

1454
00:53:35,907 --> 00:53:37,181
(Losing her mind)

1455
00:53:37,307 --> 00:53:39,307
This is so romantic.

1456
00:53:39,967 --> 00:53:42,019
Oh, my. This is nice.

1457
00:53:42,614 --> 00:53:43,854
Yes.

1458
00:53:44,181 --> 00:53:46,525
(Laughing)

1459
00:53:46,695 --> 00:53:49,135
I wish nighttime would never come
and it could just stay like this all day.

1460
00:53:49,160 --> 00:53:51,228
- Wouldn't it be scary at night?
- I think so too.

1461
00:53:51,229 --> 00:53:53,363
We might hear a lot of animals at night.

1462
00:53:53,825 --> 00:53:57,034
There are no doors. It's all open.

1463
00:53:57,283 --> 00:53:59,856
Monkeys can come in and take something
while we're sleeping.

1464
00:53:59,857 --> 00:54:00,838
We should be careful.

1465
00:54:01,376 --> 00:54:04,670
(Orangutans also pop up
from time to time.)

1466
00:54:05,363 --> 00:54:07,888
(They roam freely through the trees...)

1467
00:54:08,654 --> 00:54:12,608
(and all around the area.)

1468
00:54:15,388 --> 00:54:18,001
(Take good care of your backpack.)

1469
00:54:18,168 --> 00:54:20,706
- How about snakes?
- Even if you see them, that's fine.

1470
00:54:20,866 --> 00:54:23,139
Just put them in your mouths.

1471
00:54:23,692 --> 00:54:25,629
Is that everything?

1472
00:54:26,029 --> 00:54:27,704
- It's here.
- Where?

1473
00:54:27,705 --> 00:54:29,633
This is everything.

1474
00:54:29,705 --> 00:54:31,492
- All we have is one backpack.
- One bag.

1475
00:54:31,493 --> 00:54:32,703
We're compact.

1476
00:54:32,732 --> 00:54:33,831
One bag for four people.

1477
00:54:33,832 --> 00:54:35,806
You have one bag for yourself.

1478
00:54:35,825 --> 00:54:37,441
- Why?
- Why?

1479
00:54:37,472 --> 00:54:38,558
I don't know.

1480
00:54:38,618 --> 00:54:39,777
Ask him.

1481
00:54:40,825 --> 00:54:41,778
Hello.

1482
00:54:42,725 --> 00:54:44,825
Why do they share one bag?

1483
00:54:45,198 --> 00:54:46,638
(Satisfying)

1484
00:54:46,671 --> 00:54:48,684
- Excuse me.
- Why?

1485
00:54:48,685 --> 00:54:51,722
Even Ipu is asking why.
He finds it strange too.

1486
00:54:51,818 --> 00:54:54,024
Even though he feels at home in nature.

1487
00:54:54,071 --> 00:54:55,192
Not enough.

1488
00:54:55,193 --> 00:54:56,627
Right. It's not enough.

1489
00:54:57,923 --> 00:55:00,731
Even the nature man has one bag.

1490
00:55:01,518 --> 00:55:04,071
(They're more minimalist
than someone living in nature.)

1491
00:55:04,305 --> 00:55:06,069
I'm so sweaty, I want to get in the water.

1492
00:55:06,403 --> 00:55:07,938
Let's go for a swim.

1493
00:55:08,171 --> 00:55:09,445
Let's shower there.

1494
00:55:09,446 --> 00:55:10,607
- Okay.
- Really?

1495
00:55:10,785 --> 00:55:11,777
- Let's go.
- Sounds good.

1496
00:55:11,831 --> 00:55:14,178
- Right away.
- Go now.

1497
00:55:14,718 --> 00:55:15,758
What did you say?

1498
00:55:15,831 --> 00:55:17,014
- "Go now."
- "Go now."

1499
00:55:17,065 --> 00:55:18,911
We're just saying, "Let's go."

1500
00:55:18,938 --> 00:55:21,118
- Let's go. Go now.
- Go now.

1501
00:55:21,445 --> 00:55:22,696
(He learned quickly.)

1502
00:55:23,787 --> 00:55:25,856
<i>Go now</i>

1503
00:55:26,816 --> 00:55:29,962
(Today's shower spot is the river
they just crossed.)

1504
00:55:29,975 --> 00:55:32,362
- Gosh!
- We're here.

1505
00:55:32,763 --> 00:55:34,131
Let's go in.

1506
00:55:37,267 --> 00:55:39,403
The water looks blue.

1507
00:55:39,903 --> 00:55:42,039
Let's take our shoes off and jump in!

1508
00:55:42,372 --> 00:55:43,440
Let's go!

1509
00:55:43,534 --> 00:55:44,808
- Let's go!
- Bamboo!

1510
00:55:44,809 --> 00:55:46,577
What is that? I want to ride on that.

1511
00:55:46,702 --> 00:55:47,978
What is that?

1512
00:55:48,069 --> 00:55:50,581
- Awesome.
- That's cool.

1513
00:55:50,736 --> 00:55:52,736
It's refreshing.

1514
00:55:52,983 --> 00:55:54,218
I'm going in.

1515
00:55:54,756 --> 00:55:56,822
(Getting ready to get in the water)

1516
00:55:58,342 --> 00:56:02,829
(Running into the water)

1517
00:56:03,049 --> 00:56:04,294
Wait. I'm drifting away.

1518
00:56:06,278 --> 00:56:07,931
(A cold shower)

1519
00:56:07,932 --> 00:56:09,846
- I'm drifting away.
- It's carrying me away.

1520
00:56:09,871 --> 00:56:12,026
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye!

1521
00:56:12,620 --> 00:56:15,072
We're throwing off all the shackles
of the world,

1522
00:56:15,273 --> 00:56:18,208
and heading back to Korea.

1523
00:56:19,776 --> 00:56:21,745
There's a monkey over there.

1524
00:56:21,950 --> 00:56:22,980
Where?

1525
00:56:23,023 --> 00:56:24,381
It stopped.

1526
00:56:24,382 --> 00:56:26,030
(There are monkeys everywhere you look.)

1527
00:56:26,483 --> 00:56:27,784
Your butt.

1528
00:56:28,418 --> 00:56:30,053
Your butt looks huge.

1529
00:56:31,703 --> 00:56:34,410
(Her butt is filled with air.)

1530
00:56:35,257 --> 00:56:36,877
You're farting.

1531
00:56:39,030 --> 00:56:42,534
(Splashing around
with just their faces above the surface)

1532
00:56:42,868 --> 00:56:44,868
Harimu is here.

1533
00:56:44,928 --> 00:56:46,670
Harimu, come on in.

1534
00:56:46,671 --> 00:56:48,534
- I'm back.
- Come on.

1535
00:56:52,812 --> 00:56:56,599
(Playing and showering at the same time)

1536
00:56:57,463 --> 00:57:00,637
Her waacking is crazy.

1537
00:57:01,057 --> 00:57:02,363
(Twerking)

1538
00:57:02,943 --> 00:57:04,857
(A new skill, twerking in the water!)

1539
00:57:05,517 --> 00:57:08,108
(Twerking for the members again)

1540
00:57:08,681 --> 00:57:12,147
(Satisfied)

1541
00:57:12,148 --> 00:57:13,163
That's so funny.

1542
00:57:13,181 --> 00:57:15,465
Is it okay to wash your hair
with just water?

1543
00:57:15,675 --> 00:57:16,800
I think so.

1544
00:57:17,100 --> 00:57:18,535
It's super cold.

1545
00:57:19,913 --> 00:57:21,972
It's waking me up. My brain!

1546
00:57:22,179 --> 00:57:23,326
I can feel my brain.

1547
00:57:23,653 --> 00:57:25,113
- It's so cold.
- I can feel my brain.

1548
00:57:25,114 --> 00:57:28,126
- I can really feel my brain.
- Let me wash your hair.

1549
00:57:28,599 --> 00:57:30,847
- My brain feels alive.
- Let me massage your head.

1550
00:57:33,493 --> 00:57:35,185
It's so refreshing.

1551
00:57:36,599 --> 00:57:38,021
Ma'am.

1552
00:57:38,022 --> 00:57:40,299
Let me give you a head massage.

1553
00:57:40,545 --> 00:57:42,993
- A head massage for you too.
- Thank you.

1554
00:57:43,405 --> 00:57:45,285
(The water is nice, and Sian is kind.)

1555
00:57:45,319 --> 00:57:47,130
I feel so free.

1556
00:57:47,152 --> 00:57:49,900
- This is paradise.
- Really.

1557
00:57:51,468 --> 00:57:54,805
Then you get up and see nature.

1558
00:57:55,305 --> 00:57:56,940
You can see nature in every direction.

1559
00:57:57,240 --> 00:58:00,043
- Nature on the side too.
- The view is stunning.

1560
00:58:00,044 --> 00:58:01,378
The perfect view for a mountain spirit.

1561
00:58:03,160 --> 00:58:04,481
Aren't we like fairies now?

1562
00:58:05,382 --> 00:58:06,950
I'll wash this too.

1563
00:58:07,551 --> 00:58:09,904
Woodcutter! Don't steal my clothes.

1564
00:58:09,905 --> 00:58:12,723
- You're watching us!
- Woodcutter!

1565
00:58:12,831 --> 00:58:14,091
Don't steal my clothes.

1566
00:58:14,092 --> 00:58:16,593
- You're so mean.
- Okay?

1567
00:58:16,689 --> 00:58:19,663
- Even if you like me, don't steal it.
- Don't steal it.

1568
00:58:21,049 --> 00:58:23,256
What's the purpose of this swimming?

1569
00:58:23,283 --> 00:58:24,434
Don't steal it.

1570
00:58:25,135 --> 00:58:26,937
We've become nature people.

1571
00:58:28,920 --> 00:58:31,147
(Scooping)

1572
00:58:31,462 --> 00:58:32,576
It's really refreshing.

1573
00:58:33,256 --> 00:58:35,445
Harimu washes her face
in an interesting way.

1574
00:58:36,680 --> 00:58:39,410
(The queen doesn't lower her head
to wash her face.)

1575
00:58:39,656 --> 00:58:42,690
(Standing)

1576
00:58:45,177 --> 00:58:47,557
- It's so nice.
- It's refreshing.

1577
00:58:48,291 --> 00:58:50,316
I feel like I'm at an outdoor hot spring.

1578
00:58:50,747 --> 00:58:52,029
A cold spring.

1579
00:58:52,397 --> 00:58:53,797
A cold spring?

1580
00:58:54,531 --> 00:58:56,557
- It looks good. What is it?
- I don't know what it is.

1581
00:58:56,558 --> 00:58:57,701
Let's sit down and eat.

1582
00:58:57,751 --> 00:58:59,036
Okay.

1583
00:58:59,836 --> 00:59:00,737
Hey!

1584
00:59:01,338 --> 00:59:02,472
Hey!

1585
00:59:05,418 --> 00:59:07,077
- Hey!
- It stole our food.

1586
00:59:07,125 --> 00:59:08,278
Hey!

1587
00:59:08,511 --> 00:59:09,880
Hey, that's mine!

1588
00:59:10,091 --> 00:59:11,998
- Gosh.
- That was mine!

1589
00:59:12,025 --> 00:59:14,384
- Give it back!
- What did it take?

1590
00:59:14,518 --> 00:59:15,731
Our food.

1591
00:59:15,971 --> 00:59:17,971
It wasn't scared at all.

1592
00:59:18,745 --> 00:59:20,418
(Collecting)

1593
00:59:20,445 --> 00:59:22,259
They just eat everything.

1594
00:59:22,444 --> 00:59:23,553
- They're not picky.
- We have one more.

1595
00:59:23,894 --> 00:59:26,493
- What is this?
- Fried sweet potato?

1596
00:59:26,494 --> 00:59:27,727
(Trying the snack later than the monkey)

1597
00:59:27,980 --> 00:59:29,666
Let me pour it.

1598
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:33,370
- It reminds me of makgeolli.
- Right.

1599
00:59:34,481 --> 00:59:36,573
- A cup of tea?
- It's coffee.

1600
00:59:37,140 --> 00:59:38,542
A warm coffee.

1601
00:59:38,567 --> 00:59:40,444
You need hot coffee at a time like this.

1602
00:59:40,474 --> 00:59:43,061
I usually prefer iced coffee,
but I want hot coffee now.

1603
00:59:43,062 --> 00:59:45,916
Wait. We have sugar here.

1604
00:59:46,578 --> 00:59:48,151
You can add it if you want.

1605
00:59:49,219 --> 00:59:51,711
- If you like coffee, add some.
- Yes.

1606
00:59:52,265 --> 00:59:53,890
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1607
00:59:55,098 --> 00:59:57,576
(Slurping)

1608
00:59:57,796 --> 00:59:59,096
It's good.

1609
00:59:59,310 --> 01:00:00,410
(Slurping)

1610
01:00:00,630 --> 01:00:02,264
Wow.

1611
01:00:02,599 --> 01:00:04,667
I think this coffee's
naturally a little sweet.

1612
01:00:04,668 --> 01:00:07,202
Yeah. I love it.

1613
01:00:07,437 --> 01:00:09,304
- It's a bit toasty.
- It tastes just like scorched rice.

1614
01:00:09,305 --> 01:00:10,339
It's so good.

1615
01:00:10,574 --> 01:00:11,407
What's this?

1616
01:00:11,608 --> 01:00:12,675
Shall we try this?

1617
01:00:13,310 --> 01:00:14,310
Fried bananas?

1618
01:00:14,945 --> 01:00:18,481
(Trying it immediately.)

1619
01:00:18,582 --> 01:00:20,216
Fried sweet potatoes!
Fried sweet pumpkins!

1620
01:00:20,217 --> 01:00:20,950
- Sweet pumpkins?
- Sweet potatoes!

1621
01:00:20,951 --> 01:00:21,851
It's so good.

1622
01:00:23,086 --> 01:00:24,119
It tastes like fries.

1623
01:00:24,120 --> 01:00:25,020
Wow!

1624
01:00:25,021 --> 01:00:26,155
- It's good, right?
- So crunchy.

1625
01:00:27,391 --> 01:00:28,658
It's sweet and savory.

1626
01:00:32,162 --> 01:00:33,395
They seasoned it.

1627
01:00:33,597 --> 01:00:34,664
Mmm!

1628
01:00:34,665 --> 01:00:35,698
It's so good.

1629
01:00:36,099 --> 01:00:36,965
Yeah.

1630
01:00:37,501 --> 01:00:39,135
I can see why the monkeys took it.

1631
01:00:40,203 --> 01:00:41,703
Something even monkeys want.

1632
01:00:42,139 --> 01:00:43,305
- They took a lot.
- Like four.

1633
01:00:43,306 --> 01:00:44,640
Four or six, I think.

1634
01:00:44,641 --> 01:00:45,541
- So greedy.
- They took a lot.

1635
01:00:45,542 --> 01:00:46,342
(A warm treat even the monkeys
can't resist.)

1636
01:00:46,543 --> 01:00:48,611
We have nothing to do now.

1637
01:00:48,612 --> 01:00:49,912
Our phones have no connection.

1638
01:00:50,647 --> 01:00:53,282
When it gets dark,
we won't even have that.

1639
01:00:53,283 --> 01:00:54,883
- Lamps.
- No lights.

1640
01:00:54,884 --> 01:00:56,051
- What do we do now?
- Oh, no.

1641
01:00:56,820 --> 01:00:58,554
We really have nothing to do.

1642
01:00:58,989 --> 01:01:00,288
(Staring)

1643
01:01:00,289 --> 01:01:03,259
You guys totally look like a hiking club.

1644
01:01:04,027 --> 01:01:06,795
This would be perfect for a dating show.

1645
01:01:06,796 --> 01:01:08,030
No. 1, 2, 3, 4.

1646
01:01:08,031 --> 01:01:09,298
Then...

1647
01:01:09,433 --> 01:01:10,833
We've got nothing else to do.

1648
01:01:10,834 --> 01:01:12,168
So let's film a dating show.

1649
01:01:12,402 --> 01:01:14,837
We've got five ladies and five gents here.

1650
01:01:14,838 --> 01:01:15,836
Damn.

1651
01:01:15,837 --> 01:01:18,941
Let's be honest. Is there anyone here...

1652
01:01:18,942 --> 01:01:20,743
getting a little boost from anyone?

1653
01:01:23,713 --> 01:01:26,848
Is anyone making this journey
a little easier?

1654
01:01:26,849 --> 01:01:27,949
(And no one found their motivation.)

1655
01:01:27,950 --> 01:01:28,822
Hands up!

1656
01:01:30,020 --> 01:01:31,721
Nothing gives me a dopamine rush
like romance.

1657
01:01:31,722 --> 01:01:33,656
- A show within a show.
- Yeah.

1658
01:01:33,657 --> 01:01:35,024
(An evening in the jungle
with no electricity or dopamine.)

1659
01:01:35,258 --> 01:01:37,759
As soon as we get down tomorrow,
I'm heading straight to the laundromat.

1660
01:01:37,760 --> 01:01:41,697
(Hanging wet clothes.)

1661
01:01:42,265 --> 01:01:43,432
Are you heading to that table?

1662
01:01:43,834 --> 01:01:45,001
Are you getting closer?

1663
01:01:45,268 --> 01:01:46,402
Are you sitting there?

1664
01:01:46,403 --> 01:01:48,770
Are you going for her?

1665
01:01:48,771 --> 01:01:52,107
(Squeezing dopamine)

1666
01:01:52,943 --> 01:01:56,045
(Happy)

1667
01:01:57,080 --> 01:02:03,318
(They chat away until sunset.)

1668
01:02:04,221 --> 01:02:06,823
(Meanwhile, Ipu is preparing
something for them.)

1669
01:02:07,724 --> 01:02:11,393
(Handmade from jungle wood)

1670
01:02:11,795 --> 01:02:13,863
(Crackle)

1671
01:02:14,598 --> 01:02:16,032
Ooh, a campfire.

1672
01:02:16,299 --> 01:02:17,099
Now that's a fire!

1673
01:02:17,100 --> 01:02:18,133
(Ipu's cozy campfire)

1674
01:02:18,134 --> 01:02:20,035
Wow, that fire's really roaring.

1675
01:02:20,036 --> 01:02:21,436
You can hear it roaring.

1676
01:02:22,405 --> 01:02:23,805
- This feels nice.
- So nice.

1677
01:02:24,541 --> 01:02:25,641
I love this vibe.

1678
01:02:25,642 --> 01:02:29,812
Campfire show.

1679
01:02:29,813 --> 01:02:30,913
(The fire burns bright as night falls.)

1680
01:02:32,015 --> 01:02:34,383
What was the highlight of the day
for everyone?

1681
01:02:34,384 --> 01:02:36,652
I honestly thought...

1682
01:02:36,653 --> 01:02:38,320
I'd be drenched in sweat.

1683
01:02:38,321 --> 01:02:39,989
But the weather was surprisingly nice.

1684
01:02:39,990 --> 01:02:43,192
- It was a healing course.
- I agree.

1685
01:02:43,193 --> 01:02:44,159
(Beautiful weather made the trek
all the more relaxing.)

1686
01:02:44,194 --> 01:02:46,328
Ipu was...

1687
01:02:46,329 --> 01:02:48,764
such a perfect guide.

1688
01:02:48,765 --> 01:02:49,832
Totally.

1689
01:02:50,033 --> 01:02:52,401
When Ipu first came to us and said,

1690
01:02:52,802 --> 01:02:54,236
"Let's go to the jungle."

1691
01:02:54,638 --> 01:02:56,038
That moment.

1692
01:02:56,406 --> 01:02:58,207
And the moment he said
we'd be sleeping in there.

1693
01:02:58,208 --> 01:02:59,109
- We were like, what?
- What?

1694
01:03:00,243 --> 01:03:02,845
(During today's breakfast)

1695
01:03:02,946 --> 01:03:05,147
Let me explain a little about the jungle.

1696
01:03:06,116 --> 01:03:08,017
Wow!

1697
01:03:08,885 --> 01:03:10,285
(We didn't think we'd go to a jungle.)

1698
01:03:10,654 --> 01:03:13,222
- That was a terrifying moment.
- Yeah.

1699
01:03:13,223 --> 01:03:14,790
Seriously, why are we even here?

1700
01:03:15,258 --> 01:03:17,893
After having such a nice breakfast
at the resort this morning.

1701
01:03:17,894 --> 01:03:19,995
I know, right? That place was fire.

1702
01:03:20,830 --> 01:03:21,630
It's dinner!

1703
01:03:21,932 --> 01:03:22,965
(Turning)

1704
01:03:23,667 --> 01:03:25,668
(And just in time, dinner is served.)

1705
01:03:25,669 --> 01:03:26,669
Dinner time!

1706
01:03:27,137 --> 01:03:28,137
It looks so good!

1707
01:03:28,538 --> 01:03:30,539
(Can't help but clap.)

1708
01:03:31,541 --> 01:03:33,575
It's full Indonesian style.

1709
01:03:33,677 --> 01:03:35,344
How did they even cook all this?

1710
01:03:36,346 --> 01:03:37,346
Curry!

1711
01:03:38,415 --> 01:03:40,015
Wow, these look amazing.

1712
01:03:40,016 --> 01:03:42,418
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1713
01:03:43,153 --> 01:03:44,520
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

1714
01:03:44,521 --> 01:03:46,489
(The full dinner spread is ready.)

1715
01:03:46,490 --> 01:03:48,491
I'm going for curry.

1716
01:03:48,726 --> 01:03:50,659
I love curry.

1717
01:03:50,660 --> 01:03:51,960
(Won Ji goes for curry first.)

1718
01:03:52,295 --> 01:03:53,896
This curry's really thin.

1719
01:03:53,897 --> 01:03:55,464
Yeah, it's very soupy.

1720
01:03:55,465 --> 01:03:56,465
(Almost like soup)

1721
01:03:57,067 --> 01:03:59,235
(Mix it all up.)

1722
01:04:00,003 --> 01:04:02,338
(And dig right in.)

1723
01:04:02,339 --> 01:04:04,340
(Another bite)

1724
01:04:04,608 --> 01:04:07,677
As a curry lover, how's Indonesian curry?

1725
01:04:07,678 --> 01:04:09,779
It's not as curry-like.

1726
01:04:09,780 --> 01:04:12,548
It's got a hint of curry.

1727
01:04:13,216 --> 01:04:15,217
But it's pretty thin
and really heavy on the spices.

1728
01:04:16,920 --> 01:04:17,786
It's good.

1729
01:04:19,522 --> 01:04:21,022
This looks good too. What is it?

1730
01:04:21,023 --> 01:04:22,524
I think it's like braised chicken.

1731
01:04:24,127 --> 01:04:25,761
(Nom)

1732
01:04:26,796 --> 01:04:27,596
Mmm.

1733
01:04:27,597 --> 01:04:28,663
This is so good!

1734
01:04:28,664 --> 01:04:29,564
- Is it good?
- Yes.

1735
01:04:29,734 --> 01:04:31,000
Are you talking about this one?

1736
01:04:31,167 --> 01:04:32,100
Okay.

1737
01:04:32,101 --> 01:04:33,602
(Savory chicken, stir-fried with spices.)

1738
01:04:33,870 --> 01:04:35,370
Let me try some.

1739
01:04:35,739 --> 01:04:37,473
(Nom)

1740
01:04:37,474 --> 01:04:40,042
It's like an Indonesian version
of spicy braised chicken.

1741
01:04:40,043 --> 01:04:40,976
(You're right.)

1742
01:04:40,977 --> 01:04:42,278
I think this is tofu.

1743
01:04:42,646 --> 01:04:45,014
(Sian's on a roll,
trying yet another dish.)

1744
01:04:47,083 --> 01:04:48,016
It's good!

1745
01:04:48,551 --> 01:04:49,284
Tofu.

1746
01:04:49,285 --> 01:04:50,485
(Her foodie buddy grabs some right away.)

1747
01:04:50,920 --> 01:04:51,586
It's good, isn't it?

1748
01:04:51,587 --> 01:04:52,588
(Their tastes are in sync.)

1749
01:04:52,589 --> 01:04:54,423
- It's so good.
- A little like gochujang.

1750
01:04:54,424 --> 01:04:55,390
It's very Korean.

1751
01:04:55,659 --> 01:04:59,362
They all have this underlying flavor.

1752
01:04:59,629 --> 01:05:01,597
It's got this hint of...

1753
01:05:02,032 --> 01:05:03,999
Sichuan pepper throughout.

1754
01:05:04,968 --> 01:05:05,935
I absolutely love it.

1755
01:05:06,569 --> 01:05:07,502
(Haha)

1756
01:05:07,537 --> 01:05:09,037
I love it too.

1757
01:05:09,239 --> 01:05:10,739
Why's Indonesian food so good?

1758
01:05:11,508 --> 01:05:12,441
What's this?

1759
01:05:13,076 --> 01:05:13,976
Tofu?

1760
01:05:13,977 --> 01:05:15,544
(Meanwhile, Harimu tries a new dish.)

1761
01:05:16,413 --> 01:05:17,946
No way.

1762
01:05:18,214 --> 01:05:20,850
Potato croquette!

1763
01:05:21,651 --> 01:05:22,784
(Nom)

1764
01:05:22,785 --> 01:05:24,820
- Potato croquette.
- Sounds delicious.

1765
01:05:26,256 --> 01:05:27,723
Okay!

1766
01:05:29,192 --> 01:05:32,227
(Croquette feast begins.)

1767
01:05:32,562 --> 01:05:34,496
It's croquettes and nothing else for her.

1768
01:05:35,331 --> 01:05:37,032
(Gabee tries the croquettes too.)

1769
01:05:37,033 --> 01:05:38,834
- It's really salty.
- Which one?

1770
01:05:39,336 --> 01:05:41,904
- This.
- Yeah.

1771
01:05:43,540 --> 01:05:45,441
(Balance out the saltiness
with some shrimp chips.)

1772
01:05:45,442 --> 01:05:47,877
(Crunch)

1773
01:05:48,778 --> 01:05:50,278
It tastes so good
after being in the water.

1774
01:05:50,513 --> 01:05:51,379
Yeah.

1775
01:05:51,848 --> 01:05:52,981
It's so good.

1776
01:05:52,982 --> 01:05:53,849
(Nom)

1777
01:05:54,150 --> 01:05:58,353
(Digging into the jungle buffet.)

1778
01:05:58,655 --> 01:05:59,622
Honestly...

1779
01:06:00,357 --> 01:06:03,359
I didn't think
we'd get to feast like this.

1780
01:06:03,827 --> 01:06:06,028
I think we're all eating better here
than we do outside.

1781
01:06:06,029 --> 01:06:08,497
They even gave us snacks.

1782
01:06:08,699 --> 01:06:10,499
It's almost like a resort.

1783
01:06:11,368 --> 01:06:12,868
An all-inclusive.

1784
01:06:14,037 --> 01:06:16,405
The fire makes it smell like
we're out in the country.

1785
01:06:16,773 --> 01:06:17,640
(Thunder)

1786
01:06:17,641 --> 01:06:18,874
Whoa, thunder and lightning!

1787
01:06:19,209 --> 01:06:21,610
- Rumble!
- No way.

1788
01:06:21,611 --> 01:06:22,945
I think it's going to rain soon.

1789
01:06:22,946 --> 01:06:24,346
Why is there always lightning here?

1790
01:06:24,781 --> 01:06:25,547
I know, right?

1791
01:06:25,949 --> 01:06:27,782
Let's talk about...

1792
01:06:27,783 --> 01:06:29,050
our first impressions of each other.

1793
01:06:29,753 --> 01:06:31,053
- I like that.
- Oh, wow.

1794
01:06:31,054 --> 01:06:32,888
(There's always one person
who's into this stuff.)

1795
01:06:33,123 --> 01:06:34,824
I've known Gabee...

1796
01:06:35,358 --> 01:06:37,893
- for about 10 years.
- Oh, really?

1797
01:06:37,894 --> 01:06:41,030
- You were her student, right?
- Yes.

1798
01:06:41,031 --> 01:06:42,464
Being able to finally...

1799
01:06:42,465 --> 01:06:44,233
see her as an older sister on this trip...

1800
01:06:44,234 --> 01:06:46,501
means a lot to me.

1801
01:06:46,904 --> 01:06:49,305
It feels weird.
She's technically my teacher.

1802
01:06:49,306 --> 01:06:51,507
- Ms. Gabee!
- But I wanted us to be like sisters.

1803
01:06:51,841 --> 01:06:53,775
That's what I wanted on the first day.

1804
01:06:54,010 --> 01:06:56,511
But from day one,
she made me feel really comfortable.

1805
01:06:57,313 --> 01:06:59,147
She said, "It might feel awkward,
but just think of me as your big sister."

1806
01:06:59,148 --> 01:07:00,615
And I could tell she really meant it.

1807
01:07:00,817 --> 01:07:03,618
- You were touched.
- It was so sincere.

1808
01:07:03,720 --> 01:07:04,687
Yeah.

1809
01:07:04,688 --> 01:07:08,290
That's right. I thought you'd feel
a little uncomfortable.

1810
01:07:08,291 --> 01:07:09,825
I was so worried about that.

1811
01:07:09,826 --> 01:07:12,094
- Since you two are in the same field.
- Exactly.

1812
01:07:12,095 --> 01:07:14,262
- She's kind of senior.
- Of course.

1813
01:07:14,263 --> 01:07:15,631
And honestly,

1814
01:07:15,999 --> 01:07:17,901
I think the dance scene...

1815
01:07:17,902 --> 01:07:20,970
really needs someone like her.

1816
01:07:21,271 --> 01:07:22,938
I mean it.

1817
01:07:23,339 --> 01:07:24,639
I mean every word.

1818
01:07:24,807 --> 01:07:26,175
We need a dance star!

1819
01:07:26,609 --> 01:07:28,310
- Dance star.
- I mean it.

1820
01:07:28,311 --> 01:07:32,013
- We're going to be dance stars!
- Yes! Okay!

1821
01:07:32,014 --> 01:07:34,083
The next dance stars.

1822
01:07:34,084 --> 01:07:35,016
I'd seen Gabee...

1823
01:07:35,585 --> 01:07:38,020
plenty of times before.

1824
01:07:38,021 --> 01:07:40,455
- We met on "World Dice Tour" too.
- Yeah.

1825
01:07:40,657 --> 01:07:42,191
She's really thoughtful...

1826
01:07:42,859 --> 01:07:44,526
- and always looks out for people.
- So true.

1827
01:07:44,794 --> 01:07:46,995
I realized I hadn't been wrong
about her after all.

1828
01:07:47,231 --> 01:07:48,897
That's our queen Gabee!

1829
01:07:48,898 --> 01:07:49,932
(Laughing)

1830
01:07:50,233 --> 01:07:53,302
You really sound like a true fan!

1831
01:07:53,603 --> 01:07:54,703
That's our queen!

1832
01:07:56,105 --> 01:07:58,640
As for Sian...

1833
01:07:59,042 --> 01:08:02,311
At first, I wasn't sure if Sian
and I would really get along.

1834
01:08:02,579 --> 01:08:03,946
Oh, why?

1835
01:08:03,947 --> 01:08:06,582
Because...

1836
01:08:06,583 --> 01:08:09,685
I'd seen her clash with some
of the girls on "Single's Inferno."

1837
01:08:10,320 --> 01:08:11,954
(She thought Sian was a total ice queen.)

1838
01:08:11,955 --> 01:08:14,256
- Darn!
- But!

1839
01:08:14,324 --> 01:08:15,391
She was like, "Gabee!"

1840
01:08:15,392 --> 01:08:17,359
Yeah.

1841
01:08:17,360 --> 01:08:19,094
Was I like this?

1842
01:08:19,095 --> 01:08:20,129
That's the vibe she gave me.

1843
01:08:20,130 --> 01:08:22,531
She was totally giving
little sister vibes.

1844
01:08:22,532 --> 01:08:23,432
Yeah.

1845
01:08:23,433 --> 01:08:24,300
And she's so nice.

1846
01:08:25,269 --> 01:08:26,368
(Blushing)

1847
01:08:26,669 --> 01:08:27,502
So nice.

1848
01:08:27,670 --> 01:08:30,505
And Sian was the last one to arrive.

1849
01:08:30,506 --> 01:08:31,306
The last one.

1850
01:08:31,307 --> 01:08:32,707
Like the wildcard.

1851
01:08:32,708 --> 01:08:34,743
- A wildcard.
- When I saw her...

1852
01:08:34,744 --> 01:08:37,046
I was like,
"Who's that gorgeous silhouette?"

1853
01:08:37,047 --> 01:08:38,480
Exactly.

1854
01:08:38,548 --> 01:08:41,350
So these two were like,
"Is she an actress?"

1855
01:08:41,351 --> 01:08:42,351
Really?

1856
01:08:42,352 --> 01:08:44,686
Then I recognized you as you got closer.

1857
01:08:44,687 --> 01:08:45,721
(Kyaaa!)

1858
01:08:45,722 --> 01:08:50,292
I felt like I could really lean on you.

1859
01:08:50,293 --> 01:08:51,827
- Right away.
- Really?

1860
01:08:52,228 --> 01:08:53,528
So, were you able to?

1861
01:08:53,529 --> 01:08:55,297
Yeah, totally!

1862
01:08:55,398 --> 01:08:57,299
May seem aloof,
but actually a total softie.

1863
01:08:57,300 --> 01:08:58,400
(Sian's actually such a sweetheart.)

1864
01:08:58,534 --> 01:09:00,468
I saw you on YouTube.

1865
01:09:00,770 --> 01:09:03,538
You're such a strong, determined person.

1866
01:09:03,706 --> 01:09:05,173
You made me realize successful people...

1867
01:09:05,174 --> 01:09:07,576
- really do have that inner strength.
- I thought that too.

1868
01:09:07,577 --> 01:09:09,612
You're so responsible.

1869
01:09:09,613 --> 01:09:12,147
- You really come off as a strong woman.
- Yeah.

1870
01:09:12,482 --> 01:09:14,183
A cute voice.

1871
01:09:14,184 --> 01:09:15,417
But a strong core.

1872
01:09:16,152 --> 01:09:16,952
(Strong)

1873
01:09:16,953 --> 01:09:18,620
- Meow.
- That's what that is.

1874
01:09:18,621 --> 01:09:20,655
When I told people
I was doing a show like this,

1875
01:09:20,890 --> 01:09:22,657
they all said,

1876
01:09:22,892 --> 01:09:25,027
"I hope Won Ji's on it."

1877
01:09:25,028 --> 01:09:26,428
"Please become friends with her!"

1878
01:09:26,429 --> 01:09:28,363
"Please!"

1879
01:09:28,364 --> 01:09:30,465
And you were actually there.

1880
01:09:30,466 --> 01:09:31,566
But you seemed a little...

1881
01:09:31,869 --> 01:09:32,734
startled.

1882
01:09:32,736 --> 01:09:34,670
- You were a little taken aback.
- Yeah.

1883
01:09:34,671 --> 01:09:36,806
- "Oh..."
- "What kind of combination is this?"

1884
01:09:36,807 --> 01:09:38,607
Yeah.
I could feel her.

1885
01:09:38,608 --> 01:09:40,776
A little surprised.

1886
01:09:40,777 --> 01:09:43,879
So I decided to approach her slowly.

1887
01:09:43,880 --> 01:09:46,448
See? She's really quick
at figuring people out.

1888
01:09:46,449 --> 01:09:48,751
That's what I thought.

1889
01:09:48,752 --> 01:09:51,019
But I feel like we really click.

1890
01:09:51,020 --> 01:09:53,321
I could totally brag about it
to my friends.

1891
01:09:53,322 --> 01:09:55,391
"We're basically besties now!"

1892
01:09:55,392 --> 01:09:56,692
- Jealous?
- Besties!

1893
01:09:56,693 --> 01:09:59,161
I think I could brag like this
when I go back.

1894
01:09:59,162 --> 01:10:00,329
You're so much fun.

1895
01:10:00,329 --> 01:10:02,978
I had only seen Harimu through Reels.

1896
01:10:02,979 --> 01:10:04,179
I'm honored.

1897
01:10:04,283 --> 01:10:06,089
I honestly thought she was a foreigner.

1898
01:10:06,709 --> 01:10:08,683
That's the best compliment.

1899
01:10:08,684 --> 01:10:10,919
- I thought you were a foreigner.
- That can happen.

1900
01:10:11,162 --> 01:10:12,954
I only knew Harimu...

1901
01:10:13,221 --> 01:10:14,923
from a distance.

1902
01:10:15,209 --> 01:10:19,494
We never really had time to get close
or get to know her personality.

1903
01:10:19,861 --> 01:10:21,763
But it turns out she is
such a great person.

1904
01:10:22,864 --> 01:10:27,068
It made me wonder why I
never took the time to get to know her.

1905
01:10:27,069 --> 01:10:28,273
I wish I had.

1906
01:10:28,274 --> 01:10:29,553
That really is a compliment.

1907
01:10:29,554 --> 01:10:31,807
It's not like I had a bad impression
of you before, but...

1908
01:10:32,228 --> 01:10:35,977
I don't really...

1909
01:10:36,014 --> 01:10:37,953
- Show your personality, right?
- Exactly.

1910
01:10:37,954 --> 01:10:38,814
I noticed.

1911
01:10:38,815 --> 01:10:41,483
I like getting to know someone
naturally over time.

1912
01:10:41,494 --> 01:10:43,694
I like meeting people naturally.

1913
01:10:43,695 --> 01:10:45,887
I strongly prefer
meeting people naturally.

1914
01:10:45,888 --> 01:10:47,622
(That's why she kept insisting
on "meeting naturally.")

1915
01:10:47,702 --> 01:10:50,125
She seemed like a purely cheerful person.

1916
01:10:50,255 --> 01:10:53,528
But I think she actually has
a lot of depth.

1917
01:10:55,188 --> 01:10:58,433
She's perceptive and capable too.

1918
01:10:58,900 --> 01:11:00,702
I highly recommend Harimu.

1919
01:11:01,294 --> 01:11:02,337
"Highly recommend?"

1920
01:11:03,205 --> 01:11:05,441
(Harimu, the youngest,
is the sisters' top pick.)

1921
01:11:05,534 --> 01:11:07,676
Would you come back
to the jungle for another trip?

1922
01:11:07,712 --> 01:11:09,311
Maybe once?

1923
01:11:09,332 --> 01:11:10,412
Once?

1924
01:11:10,559 --> 01:11:13,481
I think it'd be nice
to come with friends or family.

1925
01:11:14,299 --> 01:11:17,786
- It's a great place to actually talk.
- Exactly. People you can talk to...

1926
01:11:18,179 --> 01:11:19,621
Here's the thing.

1927
01:11:19,803 --> 01:11:22,224
Holding a "Divorce Re-Boot Camp" here.

1928
01:11:22,283 --> 01:11:23,458
That's...

1929
01:11:24,226 --> 01:11:25,694
That'd be chaos.

1930
01:11:26,294 --> 01:11:27,329
That'd be fun.

1931
01:11:27,337 --> 01:11:30,465
I think it'd also be good
for couples before marriage.

1932
01:11:30,501 --> 01:11:32,334
They could get to know
each other's personalities.

1933
01:11:32,500 --> 01:11:33,602
That'd be fun.

1934
01:11:33,603 --> 01:11:37,003
(Bukit Lawang is the perfect place
for those with big decisions to make.)

1935
01:11:37,028 --> 01:11:39,028
I want to go to the Amazon...

1936
01:11:39,674 --> 01:11:41,843
as my team is called AMAZON.

1937
01:11:41,872 --> 01:11:44,179
- True.
- I have to live up to the name.

1938
01:11:44,312 --> 01:11:47,139
I want to go there
with them at least once.

1939
01:11:47,140 --> 01:11:50,151
A mental-strength training workshop.

1940
01:11:50,239 --> 01:11:51,119
Totally.

1941
01:11:51,146 --> 01:11:53,221
Like I said earlier,

1942
01:11:53,622 --> 01:11:58,260
I never really challenged my limits.

1943
01:11:58,770 --> 01:12:02,731
I tended to always avoid them.

1944
01:12:03,170 --> 01:12:05,390
But hiking mountains,

1945
01:12:05,430 --> 01:12:07,035
going into the jungle,

1946
01:12:07,397 --> 01:12:09,271
and feeding elephants...

1947
01:12:09,272 --> 01:12:11,371
made me feel like
I had pushed past my limits.

1948
01:12:11,460 --> 01:12:14,643
So I learned and felt
so much from this trip.

1949
01:12:15,387 --> 01:12:16,378
For me,

1950
01:12:16,978 --> 01:12:19,080
I had been doubting...

1951
01:12:19,981 --> 01:12:22,250
some of my abilities.

1952
01:12:22,298 --> 01:12:23,685
- Why?
- How come?

1953
01:12:23,710 --> 01:12:24,819
(Surprised)

1954
01:12:24,945 --> 01:12:29,124
I was wondering if I was
actually a worthwhile person.

1955
01:12:30,191 --> 01:12:34,396
Then Won Ji told me I was
smart for the first time in my life.

1956
01:12:34,796 --> 01:12:36,796
You gave me so many compliments,

1957
01:12:36,829 --> 01:12:40,168
and it made me
feel like I was actually useful.

1958
01:12:40,983 --> 01:12:42,504
You're totally...

1959
01:12:42,774 --> 01:12:45,166
I really liked that about this trip.

1960
01:12:45,167 --> 01:12:48,143
Feeling like I'm valuable somewhere.

1961
01:12:49,277 --> 01:12:53,748
I usually travel a lot,

1962
01:12:53,991 --> 01:12:56,551
so I thought I was already
pretty good at packing light.

1963
01:12:57,231 --> 01:13:01,523
But I think I've learned how to get
rid of even more unnecessary baggage.

1964
01:13:02,157 --> 01:13:04,509
Was there nothing good
about spending time with us?

1965
01:13:05,413 --> 01:13:07,162
- What about us?
- What about me?

1966
01:13:07,182 --> 01:13:09,133
(The younger sisters want
to hear something from their eldest.)

1967
01:13:09,327 --> 01:13:11,399
(Gathering around)

1968
01:13:11,518 --> 01:13:14,118
I think I relied on Won Ji every moment.

1969
01:13:14,119 --> 01:13:15,136
Really?

1970
01:13:15,445 --> 01:13:19,783
Whether we were bargaining,
going somewhere, or buying something,

1971
01:13:19,784 --> 01:13:22,177
I relied on you a lot.

1972
01:13:22,205 --> 01:13:24,412
But that might have been a burden for you.

1973
01:13:24,413 --> 01:13:26,781
Yes, I think it was probably a lot.

1974
01:13:27,104 --> 01:13:28,717
I'm totally fine with that.

1975
01:13:29,690 --> 01:13:32,187
It's what I always do anyway.

1976
01:13:32,364 --> 01:13:35,290
As the oldest one in this group,

1977
01:13:36,057 --> 01:13:38,526
the trip is...

1978
01:13:38,621 --> 01:13:39,561
Are you crying?

1979
01:13:41,381 --> 01:13:43,231
- Seriously?
- Are you?

1980
01:13:47,469 --> 01:13:49,871
To be honest...

1981
01:13:54,242 --> 01:13:56,553
But you must have had such a hard time.

1982
01:13:56,554 --> 01:13:57,712
It's not that.

1983
01:13:57,713 --> 01:13:59,460
(Overwhelmed with emotion)

1984
01:14:00,221 --> 01:14:01,573
Was it really that hard?

1985
01:14:01,574 --> 01:14:03,752
It's not that it was hard.

1986
01:14:04,119 --> 01:14:05,253
I'm actually...

1987
01:14:05,887 --> 01:14:07,510
not very good at being a leader.

1988
01:14:07,534 --> 01:14:09,691
I'm never that kind of person.

1989
01:14:10,325 --> 01:14:13,547
(A moment caught
between wanting to lead the trip well,)

1990
01:14:13,637 --> 01:14:14,926
But...

1991
01:14:15,045 --> 01:14:17,378
(and doubting herself as the oldest.)

1992
01:14:17,538 --> 01:14:20,235
But I learned so much from you.

1993
01:14:20,549 --> 01:14:22,303
You're totally a natural leader.

1994
01:14:22,342 --> 01:14:24,005
You're a hardcore leader.

1995
01:14:24,582 --> 01:14:26,274
You're the ultimate leader.

1996
01:14:26,907 --> 01:14:28,155
You're at max leader level.

1997
01:14:28,179 --> 01:14:29,297
(Thank you.)

1998
01:14:29,550 --> 01:14:32,647
(The extroverted younger sisters'
way of comforting her.)

1999
01:14:32,810 --> 01:14:35,316
- It really weighed on you, right?
- I think so.

2000
01:14:35,337 --> 01:14:38,369
But she really did work hard.

2001
01:14:38,403 --> 01:14:40,955
With four people, it's a group.

2002
01:14:41,689 --> 01:14:43,992
So you probably felt
a lot of responsibility.

2003
01:14:44,096 --> 01:14:48,696
And it was our first trip
with all four of us.

2004
01:14:49,264 --> 01:14:51,599
It must've been awkward
and difficult at times.

2005
01:14:51,900 --> 01:14:54,508
But I think we each did
our part really well.

2006
01:14:54,533 --> 01:14:56,204
- Absolutely.
- That's right.

2007
01:14:56,497 --> 01:14:58,573
I'm glad there were four of us.

2008
01:14:58,967 --> 01:15:01,219
(Tight hug)

2009
01:15:01,239 --> 01:15:02,444
I love the four of us.

2010
01:15:03,705 --> 01:15:06,281
- We each have our own role.
- Absolutely.

2011
01:15:07,092 --> 01:15:08,483
It's getting hot now.

2012
01:15:10,394 --> 01:15:12,954
(The four have grown even closer.)

2013
01:15:13,788 --> 01:15:16,291
So we just have to go home
tomorrow, right?

2014
01:15:16,292 --> 01:15:17,980
(An awkward feeling suddenly settles in.)

2015
01:15:18,005 --> 01:15:19,294
We've finished eating.

2016
01:15:19,727 --> 01:15:21,296
Let's talk, play, and then sleep.

2017
01:15:21,297 --> 01:15:22,797
- Sounds good.
- Bedtime.

2018
01:15:22,872 --> 01:15:25,433
- It's really dark there.
- We shouldn't look out there.

2019
01:15:25,605 --> 01:15:28,058
It's really scary there.

2020
01:15:28,059 --> 01:15:29,971
Let's use the bathroom before bed.

2021
01:15:30,025 --> 01:15:32,173
It was a good time.

2022
01:15:32,338 --> 01:15:33,608
It's really scary.

2023
01:15:34,058 --> 01:15:36,351
- Do you think you can sleep, Harimu?
- No.

2024
01:15:36,352 --> 01:15:39,518
(After spending an even more
bonding night together)

2025
01:15:41,525 --> 01:15:44,198
(The older ones go and shower first.)

2026
01:15:44,518 --> 01:15:46,888
We have to take care
of ourselves even in the jungle.

2027
01:15:46,889 --> 01:15:47,989
Of course we do.

2028
01:15:48,178 --> 01:15:50,627
(Sian and Harimu begin
their nighttime skincare routine.)

2029
01:15:50,652 --> 01:15:54,596
We need to soothe our skin, especially
after a long day of skin irritation.

2030
01:15:54,896 --> 01:15:57,198
This doesn't feel sticky at all,

2031
01:15:57,632 --> 01:16:00,201
- and it moisturizes really well.
- I know.

2032
01:16:00,474 --> 01:16:02,937
You know how your sleep quality is better,

2033
01:16:03,167 --> 01:16:06,107
- when your skincare routine is perfect?
- Exactly.

2034
01:16:06,108 --> 01:16:10,178
You have to seal everything
in with a layer of skincare.

2035
01:16:10,561 --> 01:16:12,814
We're in the jungle right now.

2036
01:16:13,061 --> 01:16:14,082
Can you believe this?

2037
01:16:15,884 --> 01:16:17,618
Does the jungle make
our skin more hydrated?

2038
01:16:18,421 --> 01:16:21,356
Anyway, we survived.

2039
01:16:21,357 --> 01:16:24,292
We survived even the jungle.

2040
01:16:25,214 --> 01:16:27,362
- Let's go straight to bed.
- Okay.

2041
01:16:27,929 --> 01:16:29,929
And that was our
nighttime skincare routine.

2042
01:16:30,485 --> 01:16:34,169
(Sian carries her through
getting ready for bed.)

2043
01:16:34,792 --> 01:16:37,739
(After finishing their nighttime skincare,
it's finally time to sleep.)

2044
01:16:38,225 --> 01:16:41,203
(Inside the accommodation)

2045
01:16:41,470 --> 01:16:44,090
(Gabee is the first one to come in.)

2046
01:16:44,976 --> 01:16:47,248
- Let me know if you need any medicine.
- Okay.

2047
01:16:48,496 --> 01:16:49,484
(Gabee is already asleep.)

2048
01:16:49,501 --> 01:16:50,785
(Sian is also all ready for bed.)

2049
01:16:51,468 --> 01:16:55,128
(She slips into the bed beside Gabee.)

2050
01:16:57,554 --> 01:17:01,201
(Won Ji and Harimu return
from the bathroom.)

2051
01:17:01,407 --> 01:17:02,597
They're already out cold.

2052
01:17:03,314 --> 01:17:05,281
(Looking around)

2053
01:17:06,454 --> 01:17:11,365
(She fixes the mosquito nets
over Gabee and Sian.)

2054
01:17:12,079 --> 01:17:14,779
(Then gets into bed.)

2055
01:17:15,099 --> 01:17:17,745
This isn't really doing anything.

2056
01:17:18,345 --> 01:17:20,843
(Won Ji's mosquito net
seems a little off.)

2057
01:17:21,350 --> 01:17:23,737
(She just lies down.)

2058
01:17:23,937 --> 01:17:25,286
Not bad.

2059
01:17:26,087 --> 01:17:28,590
If you need to go to the bathroom,

2060
01:17:30,658 --> 01:17:32,794
just tell me.

2061
01:17:33,020 --> 01:17:35,096
That would be too rude.

2062
01:17:35,254 --> 01:17:36,297
No.

2063
01:17:37,098 --> 01:17:40,535
Then let's just agree
to do it for each other.

2064
01:17:42,346 --> 01:17:43,746
(Rustling)

2065
01:17:44,452 --> 01:17:46,885
I really can't see anything.

2066
01:17:46,886 --> 01:17:51,079
(The end of Night 7 in the jungle)

2067
01:17:53,644 --> 01:17:55,953
Harimu and I came up with a dance.

2068
01:17:56,317 --> 01:17:58,387
(Learning the Abra-ca-Empty choreography)

2069
01:17:59,973 --> 01:18:01,520
(The center with standout dance line)

2070
01:18:01,846 --> 01:18:03,073
(What's this?)

2071
01:18:03,313 --> 01:18:04,467
I got it.

2072
01:18:04,713 --> 01:18:05,633
No, you didn't.

2073
01:18:05,927 --> 01:18:07,640
You didn't. I saw everything.

2074
01:18:07,906 --> 01:18:09,387
She seems a little bossy.

2075
01:18:09,513 --> 01:18:10,853
She says you're too bossy.

2076
01:18:11,247 --> 01:18:14,985
(A special training session
just for Won Ji.)

2077
01:18:16,031 --> 01:18:18,285
(The rookie monster's
performance coming soon)

2078
01:18:18,825 --> 01:18:20,358
(Check-out day at the jungle camp)

2079
01:18:20,585 --> 01:18:22,398
Did you wash your face
and brush your teeth?

2080
01:18:22,650 --> 01:18:23,191
No, I didn't.

2081
01:18:23,498 --> 01:18:25,196
(The four have grown
much closer overnight.)

2082
01:18:25,516 --> 01:18:26,736
We're taking a taxi down.

2083
01:18:27,009 --> 01:18:28,909
(A jungle taxi made of connected tubes)

2084
01:18:29,469 --> 01:18:31,696
(Back to civilization
on the garlic-bread tube)

2085
01:18:31,992 --> 01:18:33,523
That's our first obstacle.

2086
01:18:33,729 --> 01:18:35,049
Ten seconds to launch.

2087
01:18:35,283 --> 01:18:36,934
Here we go.

2088
01:18:37,525 --> 01:18:39,600
(Wobble)

2089
01:18:39,960 --> 01:18:42,086
I'm completely soaked.
Even my underwear is soaked.

2090
01:18:42,914 --> 01:18:43,698
Ipu.

2091
01:18:45,954 --> 01:18:47,214
(Whoosh)

2092
01:18:47,540 --> 01:18:48,540
Are you okay, Ipu?

2093
01:18:51,300 --> 01:18:53,107
(Serious)

2094
01:18:53,508 --> 01:18:56,227
(An unexpected situation arises.)

2095
01:18:56,228 --> 01:18:57,733
(Is something wrong with the tube?)

2096
01:18:57,734 --> 01:18:58,861
Why is he serious again?

2097
01:18:59,280 --> 01:19:01,474
(Will they make it safely
out of the jungle?)

2098
01:19:02,894 --> 01:19:04,667
Are you okay, Harimu?

2099
01:19:04,668 --> 01:19:06,560
- You're still not feeling well, are you?
- No.

2100
01:19:06,561 --> 01:19:08,461
- Oh, no.
- Let me see.

2101
01:19:09,255 --> 01:19:11,888
She has a really high fever.
What do we do?

2102
01:19:12,475 --> 01:19:15,196
(In the end, filming is halted
and she is taken to the hospital.)

2103
01:19:15,766 --> 01:19:18,352
(Harimu developed
a high fever and abdominal pain.)

2104
01:19:19,246 --> 01:19:21,992
(It's an unfamiliar sight
from someone normally so full of energy.)

2105
01:19:22,659 --> 01:19:24,066
(What on earth happened to her?)

2106
01:19:24,067 --> 01:19:25,507
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
